window.MONARCH_CHAPTERS=(window.MONARCH_CHAPTERS||[]).concat([{"number":226,"title":"Chapter 226: Thornveil Household","paragraphs":["Meanwhile, in Everhold City, within the magnificent Thornveil Estate.","The morning sun bathed the manor in a warm golden glow.","Servants quietly carried out their duties throughout the grand residence, while gentle breezes drifted through the open corridors.","A young woman walked gracefully along one of those corridors. Her long, dark-blue hair flowed elegantly down her back, swaying gently with each step.","Clear emerald-green eyes calmly observed the path ahead.","She wore a beautiful light-blue dress embroidered with delicate silver patterns that perfectly matched her noble status.","She was none other than Ophelia Thornveil.","As she continued walking, her footsteps gradually slowed. At the end of the corridor lay a spacious balcony overlooking the vast city of Everhold.","Someone was already standing there.","A woman with sky-blue hair tied neatly into a flawless bun quietly gazed over the city below. She wore a crisp white blouse tucked into black trousers, giving her an elegant yet professional appearance.","Even without armor or robes. She naturally radiated an aura of authority.","\"Instructor Morgana.\"","Ophelia greeted respectfully.","Hearing her voice, Morgana slowly turned around.","\"Oh. Ophelia.\"","A faint smile appeared on her face.","\"Good morning.\"","\"Good morning, Instructor.\"","Ophelia walked over until she stood beside her. For a brief moment, both women silently admired the city stretching beneath them.","After several seconds, Ophelia finally spoke.","\"It’s already been four days... Has your disciple still not completed the assignment you gave him?\"","Morgana smiled helplessly.","\"No. Not yet.\"","Ever since Noah and Damien had entered the labyrinth...","Morgana had remained at the Thornveil Estate.","After concluding her discussions regarding official matters with Duke Lionel Thornveil, he had personally arranged luxurious accommodations for her within the estate.","She wasn’t particularly concerned. She trusted Damien’s judgment.","Besides the communication device she had given him remained inactive. If anything truly dangerous happened. She would know immediately.","Morgana glanced sideways at Ophelia.","\"What about you? Do you want to train again today with me? I can guide you again.\"","She asked casually.","After all Ophelia was also one of her students. The young noblewoman visibly flinched.","She instinctively took a small step backward.","\"Th-There’s no need, Instructor Morgana. I don’t want to trouble you. You are our guest.\"","Yesterday’s training session had left a lasting impression on her.","For the first time she had truly understood just how terrifying Morgana was during combat training.","Every movement had been precise. Every attack had been merciless. She never hesitated. She never held back unnecessarily. She was ruthless and brutal.","Ophelia honestly couldn’t understand how Damien endured such training every single day.","Morgana clicked her tongue.","\"Tch. Why are you looking at me as though I’m some kind of monster? Damien handles it perfectly well. He complains a lot...but he still endures it.\"","A faint smile appeared on her lips.","\"And Noah... He never complains. He’s a good boy. I have trained him few times together with my disciple.\"","The moment Noah’s name left Morgana’s lips...","Ophelia stiffened. Her emerald eyes lowered toward the floor. Her fingers unconsciously tightened into fists.","Morgana noticed the reaction immediately.","She remained silent. She knew exactly what had happened between Noah and Ophelia.","In her opinion what Noah had done in the past had unquestionably been wrong.","There was no excuse for it.","But she also believed Ophelia’s actions afterward had crossed a line. Turning an incident into a public spectacle and allowing it to destroy another person’s life.","That, too, had been wrong.","Still it wasn’t her place to interfere now. Everything was good now. Noah was improving with incredible speed. It was comparable to Damien.","The past had already happened.","\"I... I just remembered something.\"","Ophelia forced a small smile.","\"I should take my leave. See you later, Instructor.\"","Without waiting for another reply...","She quickly walked away. Her footsteps grew faster and faster. She didn’t stop until she reached her own bedroom.","Click.","The door closed behind her.","Click.","She immediately locked it. For several long moments... She simply leaned against the door.","Her breathing was uneven.","She slowly closed her eyes.","\"...Haah...\"","After calming herself slightly...","She pushed herself away and walked toward the far wall of the room.","There hung an big portrait on wall. It depicted an extraordinarily beautiful woman.","Only the upper half of her body had been painted. She wore an elegant black kimono decorated with subtle silver embroidery.","Her skin was fair and flawless. Her expression remained cold and dignified. Clear blue eyes stared calmly ahead.","Her long black hair had been tied into a graceful bun, secured by an exquisite ornamental hairpin.","The woman radiated quiet elegance.","\"...Mother.\"","Ophelia’s voice was barely above a whisper.","She stood before the portrait in silence. Her fists slowly clenched.","Then the memories returned.","She remembered that day.","The screams. The blood. The overwhelming terror. She remembered watching her mother throw herself forward to protect her.","She remembered the demon’s claws. She remembered the warmth of her mother’s embrace slowly disappearing. How she fought to the demon despite being injured. How she was devoured into the huge explosion.","At that time her father had been away, leading the battle against another group of demons.","By the time he returned. Everything had already been over.","Ophelia slowly lowered her head.","\"...I know. I know what I did was wrong.\"","Her voice trembled.","\"But... I didn’t have any other choice.\"","She slowly looked back at the portrait.","\"Father...and even Noah...had no intention of breaking off the engagement. I never loved him.\"","She shook her head weakly.","\"No... I never even liked him.\"","She closed her eyes.","\"I couldn’t accept spending the rest of my life in a marriage I never wanted.\"","A bitter smile appeared on her face.","\"But...even after everything. It still feels wrong.\"","Her voice grew quieter. Almost as though she were confessing to the only person who could no longer answer her.","Silence filled the room once again.","---","Meanwhile, Back Inside the Labyrinth.","Crunch!","Crunch!","Boom!","\"Fuck!\"","Two young men sprinted through a dense underground forest as fast as their legs could carry them.","Branches whipped against their clothes while bushes and roots blurred past beneath their feet. Behind them echoed the furious growls of monsters."]},{"number":227,"title":"Chapter 227: Labyrinth [9]","paragraphs":["Meanwhile, Back Inside the Labyrinth.","Crunch!","Crunch!","Boom!","\"Fuck!\"","Two young men sprinted through a dense underground forest as fast as their legs could carry them.","Branches whipped against their clothes while bushes and roots blurred past beneath their feet.","Behind them echoed the furious growls of monsters.","More than ten massive wolves relentlessly pursued them.","They were Direwolves—D-Rank monsters with jet-black fur, crimson eyes, and bodies nearly twice the size of ordinary wolves. Their sharp fangs protruded from their mouths as saliva dripped onto the ground while they ran.","Leading the pack was an even more terrifying beast.","A C-Rank Direwolf Alpha.","Its body was as large as a rhinoceros, covered in thick black fur with dark crimson patterns running across its limbs. Every step it took shook the ground beneath it.","Currently...","Noah and Damien had already descended to another floor of the labyrinth.","Unlike the previous floors filled with stone corridors and ancient ruins...","This floor resembled an entirely different world.","An enormous underground forest stretched endlessly beneath a cavern ceiling so high that neither of them could see it. Strange glowing vines and giant crystals embedded throughout the cavern walls served as the only source of light.","At first everything had gone surprisingly well.","They had encountered only a few weak monsters, collected several monster cores, and even managed to spend a peaceful night resting beneath a rocky cliff.","Unfortunately...","That peaceful morning hadn’t lasted long.","The scent of humans had attracted an entire Direwolf pack.","Now the starving monsters pursued them with frightening determination.","They clearly had no intention of letting their prey escape.","ROOOAAARRR!!","AWWOOOOOO!!","The Alpha let out a thunderous roar while the rest of the pack answered with deafening howls.","The forest echoed with their cries.","\"They’re still coming!\" Noah shouted while continuing to run.","\"They’re way too persistent!\" Damien replied.","The distance between them and the monsters continued shrinking.","Damien suddenly dug his foot into the ground.","\"I’ll slow them down!\"","He spun around in one smooth motion. Golden mana erupted around his sword.","The blade blazed brilliantly. With a powerful horizontal swing.","Slash!","A crescent-shaped arc of radiant light shot through the forest.","The golden slash crossed dozens of meters in an instant.","BOOM!!","It struck one of the Direwolves head-on.","The monster was thrown backward as a massive diagonal wound split open across its body.","Blood sprayed through the air before the wolf crashed violently into several trees.","Meanwhile Noah thrust both hands forward. Mana surged from his core. The earth before the charging wolves trembled.","Crack!","Crack!","A gigantic wall of crystal-blue ice erupted from the ground. Nearly five meters tall and several meters thick, it completely blocked the wolves’ path.","The monsters barely had time to react.","Boom!","Boom!","Several Direwolves slammed directly into the frozen barrier.","Bones cracked.","Some were thrown backward while others collapsed onto the ground with painful whines.","However...","Not every wolf was stopped.","The more agile Direwolves immediately leaped high into the air.","The enormous Alpha also launched itself over the wall with astonishing power.","Its massive body flew through the sky like a black meteor.","\"Tch!\"","\"They’re coming from above!\"","Damien immediately formed another magic circle.","A brilliant golden formation appeared before him.","More than five radiant spears condensed within seconds.","Light Lance!","Whoosh!","Whoosh!","Whoosh!","The blazing lances shot upward toward the airborne monsters.","Several wolves were pierced through their bodies before crashing lifelessly onto the forest floor.","Yet the Alpha twisted midair and narrowly avoided every attack before landing heavily several meters ahead.","BOOM!","The ground cracked beneath its weight.","Noah narrowed his eyes.","\"My turn.\" he said and decided to try new spell he learned while he was at home.","A deep-blue magic circle rapidly formed before him. At the same time. An identical magic circle appeared beneath one of the charging Direwolves.","\"This is... The first time I’ve used it in actual combat.\"","It was a spell he had learned only recently during his training with his mother.","A Three-Star Ice Spell.","Normally an Awakened High Core mage shouldn’t have been capable of mastering such advanced magic.","Its mana consumption was great.","However thanks to his extraordinary affinity with ice, his Adaptive Learning passive ability, and the countless hours of guidance from his mother. And lastly he possessed bloodline, Monarch of the Frost .","Noah had barely managed to learn it. Although casting it still consumed a considerable amount of mana.","His calm voice echoed through the forest.","[Crystal Bloom]","The magic circle beneath the Direwolf suddenly shone brilliantly.","Crack","A beautiful crystal flower slowly blossomed from beneath the monster’s feet. Its translucent petals shimmered with an enchanting blue glow. For a brief moment. The wolf hesitated.","Then the flower exploded.","BOOM!!","Hundreds of razor-sharp ice petals burst outward in every direction like a deadly storm.","The Direwolf didn’t even have time to scream.","Its body was shredded by countless icy blades. Blood sprayed across the surrounding trees as the monster collapsed lifelessly onto the ground.","Noah exhaled slowly.","\"So...That Crystal Bloom is pretty useful.\"","Despite the heavy mana consumption. A satisfied smile appeared on his face. Its destructive power had exceeded even his expectations.","ROOOAAARRR!!","The Direwolf Alpha let out a furious roar that shook the surrounding forest.","Despite their relentless attacks... The battle was far from over.","The Alpha was still alive.","Along with it, nearly eight D-Rank Direwolves continued charging through the forest with murderous intent.","\"They’re not giving up!\"","Damien shouted.","\"No. They’re hunting us.\"","Noah replied calmly as both of them continued sprinting between the towering trees.","There was no point in fighting the entire pack head-on. Their best option was obvious.","Kill the weaker wolves first. Then deal with the Alpha together.","Noah raised his left hand. With a single thought. More than thirty ice weapons materialized high above the battlefield.","Swords.","Spears.","Daggers.","Lances.","Each weapon floated silently before turning its razor-sharp tips toward the charging monsters below.","The wolves looked up.","But it was too late.","\"...Go.\"","The instant Noah gave the command. Every weapon descended simultaneously."]},{"number":228,"title":"Chapter 228: Labyrinth [10]","paragraphs":["Whoosh!","Whoosh!","Whoosh!","The forest echoed with countless piercing whistles.","The Direwolves scattered in every direction.","Noah intentionally focused several weapons on each individual wolf. He wasn’t interested in merely injuring them. He wanted certain kills.","Schhk!","Schhk!","Schhk!","Ice spears pierced through one Direwolf’s chest while three swords impaled another from different directions.","The two monsters collapsed immediately. They were dead.","Several more weapons struck two additional wolves.","Although they survived. Deep wounds covered their bodies, slowing their movements considerably.","Only the Alpha remained untouched. Its enormous body weaved effortlessly between the falling barrage.","Instead of retreating. It accelerated. Trees shattered as it charged straight toward Noah and Damien.","Boom!","Boom!","Its massive body crashed through trunks thick enough to require several men to encircle.","Its crimson eyes burned with savage fury.","The monster suddenly opened its gigantic jaws.","Blue mana rapidly gathered inside its mouth.","The surrounding air trembled.","\"Noah!\"","Damien immediately understood what was coming.","The next instant.","BOOM!!","A concentrated beam of blue mana erupted from the Alpha’s mouth. It tore through the forest with terrifying destructive power.","Damien instantly turned around. Golden mana exploded from his body.","His sword blazed brilliantly. It shone so brightly that it resembled a miniature sun.","Without hesitation he swung.","A massive arc of golden light collided head-on with the incoming beam.","BOOOOOOM!!","The collision produced a deafening explosion. The shockwave flattened nearby trees.","Dust and smoke engulfed the battlefield.","Damien was blown backward by the tremendous force.","His body flew several meters through the air before landing behind Noah.","\"Ghk!\"","He slid across the ground before barely managing to stop himself.","Noah clicked his tongue.","\"...Damn.\"","The gap between their strength had become even more obvious. Noah slowly stepped forward. The battlefield remained hidden beneath thick clouds of dust.","But that doesn’t mean they couldn’t kill it.","If the leader monster was alone, Damien could have kill him by now.","Right now Noah couldn’t see anything.","He took stance.","Then his breathing slowed. One emotion after another disappeared.","Excitement, fear, Impatience. Everything gradually sank into silence. The world became still. His eyes lost every trace of emotion. Only absolute focus remained.","The Second Petal.","[Still Surface Cut]","Noah calmly raised his sword. Then he performed one simple horizontal slash.","Slash.","The movement appeared ordinary.","Almost effortless. Nothing visible left his blade.","Only an invisible wave of freezing force silently traveled through the dense smoke.","A heartbeat later.","Schhk","The hidden Alpha suddenly emerged from the dust cloud. A deep horizontal wound opened across its chest.","Frost rapidly spread from the cut, freezing the surrounding flesh.","The beast let out a pained roar.","ROOOAAARRR!!","Its charging speed immediately dropped.","Seeing their leader wounded. The remaining Direwolves instinctively hesitated. That single moment was all Noah needed.","His left hand rose once again.","More ice weapons rapidly formed above the battlefield. At that exact moment. A brilliant golden slash flew past Noah from behind.","Damien had already regained his footing.","His sword shone brilliantly as another powerful attack swept across the battlefield.","\"Go!\"","Noah gave his command simultaneously.","The golden slash carved through two Direwolves with overwhelming destructive force.","Their bodies were split apart before crashing lifelessly onto the forest floor.","At the same time Noah’s rain of ice weapons descended. Multiple blades pierced the remaining wounded wolves before they could escape.","Two more monsters died instantly. Silence briefly returned to the forest.","Only three enemies remained. The Direwolf Alpha. Its chest still bleeding beneath layers of spreading frost.","And two surviving Direwolves standing protectively beside their leader. The Alpha growled viciously.","Its crimson eyes burned with hatred. Heavy breaths escaped its mouth as blood dripped onto the forest floor.","Footsteps approached from behind.","Noah glanced over his shoulder.","Damien walked toward him while resting his glowing sword across one shoulder. A confident grin spread across his face.","\"Well...This should be much easier now.\"","Noah nodded.","\"Yeah.\"","Noah tightened his grip around his sword. \"You handle the Alpha. I’ll finish the remaining two.\"","Damien’s smile widened.","\"You got it.\"","Without another word the two young men charged forward once again. Noah dashed toward the two remaining Direwolves without hesitation.","The monsters immediately locked onto him. Their crimson eyes burned with hunger and rage as they bared rows of razor-sharp fangs.","With furious growls, both wolves lunged at him simultaneously.","ROOOARRR!!","Noah remained calm. He stomped his foot against the ground. Mana surged into the earth.","The next instant.","Crack!","Massive ice spikes erupted violently from beneath the charging Direwolves.","One of the wolves reacted instantly. It pushed off the ground with powerful hind legs and leaped high into the air, narrowly escaping the deadly spikes.","The second wasn’t so fortunate.","SCHHKK!!","Several crystal-blue spikes burst upward through its body. They pierced its abdomen before tearing through its chest and back.","Fresh blood sprayed across the pristine ice, staining the crystal spikes crimson.","The metallic scent of blood spread through the surrounding forest.","The Direwolf let out a pained howl before its body went limp, hanging motionless upon the frozen spears.","It was dead.","At that exact moment the surviving wolf descended from above. Its massive claws slashed toward Noah’s head.","Clang!","Noah raised his sword just in time.","Steel collided against razor-sharp claws, producing a shower of sparks.","The impact sent vibrations through his entire arm. The Direwolf’s physical strength was tremendous.","Its muscles bulged beneath its dark fur as it continuously pushed against Noah’s blade.","But Noah was no longer the young man he had once been.","He planted his feet firmly. Mana reinforced every muscle in his body.","His grip tightened. With a sharp twist of his wrist, he redirected the wolf’s claws away from himself before taking several quick steps backward.","The instant the monster landed. A glowing blue magic circle appeared beneath its feet.","The wolf’s instincts screamed in warning.","It tried to leap away.","But it was too late. A violent storm of ice erupted from the magic circle.","Freezing winds exploded outward. Countless razor-sharp shards of ice swirled around the Direwolf like a miniature blizzard.","ROOOAAARRR!!","The monster howled in panic. Its thick fur rapidly became coated with frost as the freezing storm slashed at its body from every direction.","Blood mixed with countless ice crystals as fresh wounds appeared across its flesh.","The beast struggled desperately to escape the raging blizzard.","Meanwhile Noah calmly extended his free hand toward the sky.","Mana gathered rapidly. A gigantic spear of crystal ice materialized above him.","Its surface gleamed beneath the faint sunlight filtering through the forest canopy.","The freezing aura surrounding it caused the nearby air to shimmer.","The blizzard gradually dispersed. The wounded Direwolf finally became visible once again.","Its body was covered in deep cuts. Its movements had noticeably slowed.","Without wasting even a second. Noah thrust his hand forward.","Whooosh!","The enormous ice spear shot through the air like a bolt of frozen lightning. The DireWolf barely had time to lift its head.","SCHHKK!!","The spear pierced straight through its chest.","The tremendous force carried the monster several meters backward before pinning its lifeless body against the thick trunk of a massive tree.","Blood slowly dripped down the crystal spear.","The Direwolf’s crimson eyes dimmed.","Its body twitched once.","Then became completely still.","Noah exhaled slowly before shifting his gaze toward Damien’s battlefield.","Only the Direwolf Alpha remained.","---","The Direwolf Alpha roared furiously as it charged toward Damien one final time.","Its enormous body blurred through the forest, crushing everything in its path.","Damien remained perfectly calm.","Golden mana erupted from his body like blazing sunlight.","He tightened his grip around his sword. With a single step forward. He swung.","Slash!","A massive golden arc shot through the air. Without pausing, Damien twisted his body and unleashed another strike.","Slash!","Then a third.","Slash!","Three enormous vertical slashes tore across the battlefield one after another, each carrying overwhelming destructive force.","The Direwolf Alpha couldn’t avoid them.","BOOOOM!!","All three attacks struck its body almost simultaneously.","A deafening explosion erupted, engulfing the beast in blinding golden light.","The surrounding trees shook violently from the impact.","Dust and shattered earth were blasted into the air.","Before the smoke could settle.","Four radiant magic circles materialized high above the battlefield.","Each circle glowed with brilliant golden light.","The surrounding mana gathered rapidly before condensing into enormous spears of pure light.","Damien extended his sword toward the smoke.","\"Go.\"","The four lances descended together.","Whoooosh!!","BOOM!","BOOM!","BOOM!","BOOM!!","Each lance crashed into the Alpha with devastating force.","The repeated explosions tore apart the battlefield, leaving behind a massive crater where the monster had stood only moments earlier.","When the smoke finally dispersed...","The Direwolf Alpha lay motionless upon the shattered ground.","Its body was riddled with deep wounds, and the golden light lingering across its fur gradually faded away.","It was dead.","The forest fell silent. Only the sound of their heavy breathing remained.","Noah sheathed his sword before walking toward Damien.","\"Looks like we’re finally done.\"","Damien wiped the sweat from his forehead and let out a long breath.","\"Yeah... That pack was tougher than I expected.\"","Noah glanced at the corpses scattered across the battlefield.","\"Let’s collect their monster cores first. And after that...\"","He looked at the dead monsters thoughtfully.","\"...we’ll absorb the mana from their bodies.\"","Damien nodded without objection.","\"Sure.\"","\"We’ll take turns.\" Noah said. \"That way both of us can recover some mana before moving deeper into the labyrinth.\"","\"Sounds like a plan.\"","The two young men began moving from one corpse to another, carefully extracting the monster cores.","---","[A/N: I went to watch The Odyssey in movie theater today!! Damn, it was such a good movie. I really enjoyed it. it was a great experience!! You guys should definitely visit your nearest theater and watch it! Also, I’m poor, so this isn’t a paid review, it’s just my genuine opinion. Keke!]"]},{"number":229,"title":"Chapter 229: Duchy Of Sunweave (1)","paragraphs":["Somewhere Far Away. In South-West direction of Empire.","Holy Duchy of Sunweave.","Caeloria City","Caeloria, the capital of the Holy Duchy of Sunweave, was a city unlike any other.","Towering white buildings rose proudly into the sky, their elegant architecture blending modern craftsmanship with sacred religious traditions. Golden domes crowned many of the structures, while intricate carvings depicting the Sun God decorated their pristine marble walls.","Wide stone streets stretched throughout the city, filled with priests, knights, merchants, and pilgrims who had traveled from every corner of the continent to offer their prayers.","Yet it had everything that modern city possess.","At the very heart of the city stood its greatest landmark.","A magnificent temple of white marble and radiant gold.","Its towering spires seemed to pierce the heavens themselves, while enormous stained-glass windows reflected brilliant sunlight across the surrounding streets. Countless believers regarded it as the holiest place in the entire duchy.","Inside the temple. A vast prayer hall stretched before the entrance.","Dozens of marble pillars supported the high vaulted ceiling, and colorful sunlight poured through the stained-glass windows, bathing the hall in a warm golden glow.","At the far end stood a magnificent altar.","Behind it rose a towering white pillar engraved with the symbol of the Sun God—a brilliant golden sun whose rays spread outward in every direction.","Before the altar knelt a beautiful young woman.","She wore elegant white robes resembling those of a high priestess.","She was none other than.","Lyria Sunweave.","She knelt gracefully with both knees resting upon the polished marble floor. Her hands were clasped together in prayer. Her eyes remained gently closed.","Long blonde hair, neatly braided, rested over one shoulder, gently swaying whenever a soft breeze drifted through the temple.","The entire hall remained silent.","Only the faint sound of burning candles could be heard.","Tap.","Tap.","Tap.","Soft footsteps echoed through the prayer hall.","Hearing someone approach, Lyria slowly opened her eyes.","She rose gracefully before turning around.","A man dressed in immaculate white robes walked toward her.","His neatly combed blonde hair matched Lyria’s own, while his brilliant golden eyes seemed to shine like two miniature suns.","Although he appeared to be only in his mid-thirties, his calm demeanor carried the wisdom and dignity of someone who had lived through countless trials.","Around his neck hung a simple golden cross.","The moment his eyes met Lyria’s...","A warm, gentle smile appeared on his face.","\"Good morning, Father.\"","Lyria bowed respectfully.","The man standing before her was none other than...","Lucian Sunweave.","The Duke of the Holy Duchy of Sunweave.","And at the same time. The current Pope of the Church of the Sun God.","Lucian smiled warmly.","\"You’re here early again. When did you arrive?\"","\"I came early this morning,\" Lyria answered politely.","Lucian chuckled softly.","\"Haha... It seems my own daughter is more devoted to the Sun God than I am.\"","A faint smile appeared on Lyria’s face.","\"Oh, Father. You’re joking. I could never compare myself to you when it comes to faith.\"","Lucian laughed quietly.","Without another word, he gently placed a hand on her head and affectionately ruffled her hair.","\"You’ve always been too humble.\"","He then walked past her toward the altar. Standing before the symbol of the Sun God, Lucian closed his eyes.","He silently offered his prayers.","Lyria respectfully stepped aside and waited without uttering a single word.","Several minutes passed before Lucian finally opened his eyes.","After finishing his prayers, he turned toward his daughter.","\"Lyria. There is something important I need to discuss with you.\"","Her expression immediately became serious.","\"Of course, Father. What is it?\"","Lucian glanced around the nearly empty prayer hall.","\"...Not here. Come with me.\"","Without waiting for a response, he began walking deeper into the temple.","Lyria quietly followed behind him.","They passed through several peaceful corridors decorated with ancient murals depicting the legends of the Sun God before arriving at Lucian’s private office.","The room was spacious yet simple.","Bookshelves lined the walls, filled with countless ancient scriptures and historical records.","A sturdy wooden desk stood near the window overlooking the city.","Lucian took his seat behind the desk.","Lyria sat opposite him.","For a brief moment. Silence filled the room.","Then Lucian spoke.","\"How is your training progressing? In particular... Your Purification ability.\"","Lyria nodded.","\"It’s going well. I’m slowly becoming more proficient with Purification every day.\"","She smiled bitterly.","\"Although... The progress is painfully slow.\"","Lucian nodded with satisfaction.","\"Slow progress isn’t something to worry about. As long as you continue moving forward.\"","He looked directly into her eyes.","\"Never stop. And never neglect your training. We will need your power more than anything in the future.\"","Lyria’s expression immediately turned solemn.","\"Yes, Father. I understand. I won’t disappoint you.\"","\"Good.\"","Lucian folded his hands together upon the desk. The gentle smile that had remained on his face disappeared. His expression became unusually grave.","\"Now... The real reason I asked you to come.\"","Lyria instinctively straightened her posture.","Lucian took a slow breath before speaking.","\"We’ve identified the one who has received the Sun God’s blessing in this era. Not just normal blessing... it’s something that helps him to use Lord’s power directly, that means he would be a great hero in future.\"","Lyria’s eyes widened in disbelief.","\"...What?\"","A person personally blessed by the Sun God. There was only one reason such a miracle occurred. History had recorded it many times.","Whenever the Sun God bestowed His blessing upon a mortal. It signaled that a catastrophe capable of threatening the entire world was approaching.","The chosen individual would become humanity’s guiding light against the coming darkness.","In other words. The blessing itself was a warning.","A disaster was drawing near.","Lyria’s heartbeat quickened.","\"Father... That information is incredibly important.\"","She looked at him seriously.","\"Are you absolutely certain? Has someone truly been born with the Sun God’s blessing?\"","Lucian nodded without hesitation.","\"Yes. I am certain. I’ve actually known about him for quite some time.\"","His golden eyes narrowed slightly.","\"I simply chose not to reveal it until now.\"","Lyria fell silent.","If her father’s words were true. Then somewhere in the world. The future Hero had already begun walking the path destiny had prepared for him."]},{"number":230,"title":"Chapter 230: Duchy Of Sunweave (2)","paragraphs":["\"Father... may I know who it is?\"","Lucian smiled gently. \"Of course, my dear. That is exactly what I wanted to tell you.\"","Lyria leaned forward slightly. \"So... Who is he, Father?\"","Lucian remained silent for a few moments, as though carefully choosing his words. Finally, he spoke.","\"You already know him very well, Lyria.\"","She frowned in confusion.","\"I... know him?\"","Her mind immediately began searching through the faces of her classmates. Then one particular face surfaced in her thoughts. A young man with black hair and hazel eyes.","She had suspected it before. His extraordinary power had never seemed ordinary. But Lyria was someone who still couldn’t understand how divine energy feels. So she was unable to recognize it.","Lucian nodded before she could even ask. \"Yes.\"","\"He is in your class. His name is Damien Ashworth.\"","Lyria’s eyes widened.","Although she had already guessed the answer. Hearing it confirmed still left her stunned. \"...Damien?\"","Images of his battles flashed through her mind. The brilliant golden light. The miniature suns he could create. The overwhelming radiance that illuminated entire battlefields.","Even back then she had wondered whether such power could truly belong to an ordinary awakened individual.","Now she finally had her answer.","Lucian folded his hands together.","\"I first became interested in him after reviewing several reports from Novaris Academy. There was the incident at start of academy, then another involving a dungeon expedition... And later, the events that took place in the forests of Okahaven.\"","\"The more I read... The more curious I became. So I investigated him thoroughly. Not just him. I also reviewed the records of several outstanding students from your generation.\"","He paused briefly before continuing.","\"After learning about Damien’s abilities... I came to one conclusion. The power he possesses isn’t merely a rare talent. It is the blessing of the Sun God.\"","Lucian’s expression remained calm.","\"Even then... I wanted absolute certainty. So before your practical examination... I personally visited Novaris Academy. I observed Damien from a distance. And after seeing him with my own eyes...\"","\"My final doubts disappeared.\"","Lyria slowly nodded.","Everything finally made sense. His frightening growth. His overwhelming affinity for light.","The divine quality hidden within his mana.","\"So...\"","She looked at her father.","\"What happens now? Are you planning to bring him to the Holy Duchy?\"","Lucian immediately shook his head.","\"No. There is no need.\"","He leaned back in his chair.","\"A Hero cannot grow while being sheltered. The hardships he faces. The battles he fights. The choices he makes. Those experiences are what will shape him into the protector this world needs. If I brought him here now. I would only hinder that growth.\"","Lyria understood immediately. Heroes were forged through adversity. Not comfort.","Lucian continued.","\"Besides... If a Hero has appeared... Then destiny would never stop there.\"","His golden eyes softened.","\"Whenever a Hero is chosen. A Saintess is chosen as well.\"","Lyria nodded.","\"Yes. I’ve read about that in the ancient scriptures and stories.\"","She hesitated for a moment.","\"Do you already know who the Saintess is?\"","A gentle smile appeared on Lucian’s face.","\"Of course. I do.\"","He looked directly into her eyes. \"It’s you, my daughter.\"","For several seconds, Lyria simply blinked. Her mind went completely blank.","\"...What?\"","She stared at him in disbelief. \"F-Father... You’re joking... Aren’t you?\"","Lucian slowly shook his head. \"I’m not. There is no mistake.\"","\"You are destined to become the Saintess of this era.\"","Silence filled the office. Lyria lowered her gaze. Her thoughts raced. Everything suddenly became clear. Her extraordinary affinity for purification.","The strange warmth she had always felt whenever she prayed before the Sun God’s altar. The unknown feeling she felt while using purification ability.","None of them had been coincidences. After several moments.","She slowly lifted her head. The uncertainty in her eyes gradually disappeared. In its place only resolve remained.","\"Father... If that is truly my destiny... Then I will accept it. I am ready to become the Saintess.\"","Lucian looked at her with unmistakable pride.","A warm smile spread across his face.","\"Good. Then prepare yourself. The peaceful days you’ve enjoyed until now are coming to an end. Very soon... Your true training will begin. It will be harsher than anything you’ve ever experienced.\"","He looked at her seriously.","\"Tell me, Lyria. Are you ready?\"","Lyria slowly clenched her fists.","Determination filled her heart. Without the slightest hesitation, she answered,","\"I am.\"","The moment those words left her lips. A gentle golden radiance began to shimmer around her body. It was very light.","Her soft pink eyes glowed faintly with a warm golden hue. The air itself seemed to become calmer.","Warmer. Almost... sacred.","Lucian’s eyebrows rose slightly.","Even though the aura was still weak. He could already sense the unmistakable presence of divinity hidden within it.","A warm, gentle, and holy energy quietly flowed from Lyria’s body, filling the room with a peaceful light.","An aura that her father had recognized it years ago.","It was something she would always use unconsciously. But her father never tried to disclose it until it was right moment.","And today it was.","---","Inside the temple’s Healing Hall.","The spacious chamber was filled with rows of white beds, each prepared for wounded knights and believers seeking treatment. The scent of medicinal herbs lingered in the air, while priests and healers quietly moved about, organizing potions and healing equipment.","Lucian stood at the center of the hall, looking calmly at his daughter.","\"Lyria,\" he began, his voice firm yet gentle, \"your first task is simple.\"","He paused for a moment before continuing. \"You will heal more than two hundred people today.\"","Lyria blinked in surprise.","\"Two hundred...?\"","\"Yes.\"","Lucian nodded.","\"Most of them will be our Holy Knights.\"","A faint smile appeared on his face. \"I’ll have them spar much more intensely than usual. Naturally, many of them will be injured.\"","He folded his arms behind his back.","\"So prepare yourself.\"","Lyria took a deep breath before bowing respectfully.","\"Yes, Father.\"","There wasn’t the slightest hesitation in her voice. To many people, healing over two hundred injured individuals in a single day sounded exhausting.","To Lyria it was merely the first step. Ever since she was a little girl, she had admired the legends of the Hero and the Saintess.","The stories of those who sacrificed everything to protect humanity had inspired her more than anything else.","Now that she had learned she was destined to become the Saintess of this era... She had no intention of running away from that responsibility.","No matter how grueling the training became. No matter how many hardships awaited her...","She would endure them all. Because this was the path she had chosen. And she would walk it without regret."]},{"number":231,"title":"Chapter 231: Missing Noah?","paragraphs":["Meanwhile, Somewhere Else. Deep within another region of the Empire.","A young woman with long violet hair steadily walked through the winding tunnels of a large dungeon.","She carried an elegant bow over one shoulder, while a quiver filled with arrows rested securely against her back.","She was none other than.","Arisha Willow.","Following behind and beside her were four fellow adventurers.","Unlike the labyrinth Noah and Damien were exploring, this was an ordinary low-ranking dungeon that adventurers frequently visited to earn money and gain combat experience.","Arisha lived in Elyon City, a prosperous city located within Hayes County.","The county itself belonged to the prestigious Hayes Family.","Walking beside Arisha was a familiar young woman with brown hair tied into a neat ponytail.","It was Emma Hayes.","She glanced sideways at her friend before asking curiously,","\"What are you thinking about so deeply?\"","Arisha had remained unusually quiet ever since they entered the dungeon.","Normally, she would occasionally join the conversation or point out possible dangers ahead.","Today she simply walked forward, seemingly lost in her own thoughts.","Before Arisha could answer, one of their companions suddenly grinned.","The young man had dark burgundy hair and carried a pair of short swords at his waist.","\"Hmm... I think she’s feeling lonely.\"","Emma blinked.","\"Lonely?\"","She looked at him with confusion.","\"Ricky... what are you talking about? Why would she be lonely?\"","Before Ricky could answer, another member of the party—a young woman carrying a staff—covered her mouth with a teasing smile.","\"Oh, come on. Isn’t it obvious? Our dear Arisha hasn’t received a single call or message from her prince.\"","Emma blinked once again.","\"...Prince?\"","She looked back and forth between the three adventurers, completely confused.","What were they talking about?","After the first semester at Novaris Academy, Emma and Arisha had gradually become close friends.","Once summer vacation began, however Arisha had devoted nearly all of her time to training.","The reason wasn’t difficult to understand.","Noah Eldritch.","The boy who had once lagged far behind everyone else had suddenly risen through the rankings. By the end of the semester, he had secured second place, surpassing every student except Damien.","Even Kaelan, who had consistently ranked near the top, had fallen behind him. Had Damien not broken through to the next Core Rank during the examination.","Noah might have claimed first place. That result had deeply motivated Arisha.","Rather than feeling jealous she had simply resolved to become stronger herself. She even contacted Emma to go with her to a dungeon. To gain more experience.","Over the past three days, Emma had noticed something else. Ever since their party entered this dungeon.","Arisha had been distracted.","She often drifted into thought for no apparent reason. Now her teammates were saying she hadn’t received a message from her \"prince.\"","Emma couldn’t help becoming curious. Who exactly were they talking about?","\"Don’t listen to them. They’re just talking nonsense.\" Arisha replied calmly, though she deliberately avoided looking at anyone.","Her composed expression only made the others smile even more.","The final member of the party finally spoke. He was the oldest among them, appearing to be around twenty-three years old.","Tall and broad-shouldered, he carried an enormous greatsword across his back. Among the four adventurers accompanying them. He was undoubtedly the strongest.","With a helpless chuckle, he looked at Emma.","\"She’s talking about Noah Eldritch. Your classmate.\"","Emma’s eyes widened.","\"...What?\"","She immediately turned toward Arisha.","The violet-haired girl simply sighed, neither confirming nor denying it.","The greatsword user laughed.","\"See? I told you.\"","He folded his arms.","\"She’s been bothered ever since she stopped receiving his messages.\"","Emma looked at Arisha in disbelief.","\"Wait... You really are worried because he hasn’t contacted you?\"","She tilted her head thoughtfully before continuing,","\"But didn’t you say Noah and Damien entered a labyrinth? If I remember correctly, communication devices don’t work properly inside labyrinths because of their unstable spatial structure.\"","She gestured toward the dungeon around them.","\"It’s different from ordinary dungeons like this one. We can still make calls from here. But labyrinths interfere with long-distance communication. So isn’t that the most likely reason he hasn’t replied?\"","Emma already knew that Arisha and Noah kept in touch almost every day after summer vacation had begun.","The two frequently exchanged messages, and Noah even called her two or three times each week. Ironically, Emma hadn’t learned that from Arisha herself.","She had heard it from Lyria.","Lyria and Noah also talked regularly after the semester ended, so she naturally knew how often Noah stayed in contact with his friends.","Sometimes Emma genuinely wondered whether smartphones and social media were making people too dependent on communication.","She couldn’t understand it.","’How could people spend hours chatting through messages every single day?’","She would rather meet someone face-to-face than stare at a phone screen for half the day. Waiting for their messages.","Arisha let out a helpless sigh after noticing Emma’s expression.","\"Don’t misunderstand. I’m not distracted because I haven’t received any messages from him.\"","She looked deeper into the dim dungeon corridor ahead.","\"I was simply wondering what Noah and Damien are going through inside the labyrinth.\"","Her violet eyes became more determined.","\"I want to become strong enough to stand beside them. I want to reach their level someday.\"","Emma silently nodded.","\"...That’s true.\"","Her hand tightened around the gauntlet covering her fist.","Truthfully she felt the same. Damien had already become someone she admired. She didn’t want to keep falling behind while everyone else continued growing stronger.","Arisha glanced sideways at her before a teasing smile appeared.","\"But... I’m sure if Damien started messaging you every day...you’d happily spend hours talking to him. And you’d probably wait for his messages every single day.\"","Emma’s face instantly turned bright red.","\"W-What?! N-No! That’s not true!\"","The oldest member of the party laughed loudly.","\"So... Arisha misses Noah... And Emma misses Damien.\"","His grin widened.","\"Looks like both of you have it bad.\"","Piara, the young woman with short auburn hair, giggled mischievously.","\"Hehe... Sounds like love to me.\"","Emma’s face became even redder.","\"H-Hey! That’s absolutely not true!!\"","Her voice echoed loudly throughout the dungeon. The laughter immediately died.","Arisha’s playful expression vanished in an instant. Her golden eyes suddenly shone brightly.","Hunter’s Eyes.","Her innate ability activated automatically. The world around her became sharper.","Every movement. Every fluctuation of mana. Every distant sound. Everything became crystal clear.","She stared into the darkness far ahead. Several powerful life signatures rapidly approached.","Her expression hardened.","Without hesitation, she grabbed her bow.","\"Monsters. They’re coming.\"","The party’s relaxed atmosphere disappeared instantly.","Everyone drew their weapons.","Moments late dozens of giant lizard-like monsters burst out from the darkness. Their thick scales reflected the faint light of the dungeon crystals as they charged with savage roars.","\"They’re fast!\"","Ricky shouted.","Arisha calmly drew an arrow from her quiver. She pulled the bowstring to its limit. Dense mana rapidly gathered around the arrow until it glowed with a brilliant emerald light.","She released it.","Whoosh!","The arrow shot through the air like a streak of lightning.","Then it split apart. One arrow became many.","More than ten mana arrows formed entirely from condensed mana spread across the battlefield before raining down upon the charging monsters.","Weapon Art—Sky Hunter.","[Second Form: Thousand Feather Rain]","Although the technique normally created far more arrows.","Arisha’s current strength was still limited.","As a result, she could only produce a small number of mana arrows.","Even so each one carried deadly accuracy.","Thud!","Thud!","Thud!","Several lizard monsters collapsed before they could even reach the party.","\"Now!\"","The greatsword wielder roared. The four adventurers immediately rushed forward to intercept the remaining monsters.","Steel clashed against claws. Magic illuminated the cavern.","The battle erupted.","Meanwhile Arisha remained at the rear, continuously providing cover fire with calm precision. Even while releasing arrow after arrow. A quiet thought crossed her mind.","’...They’re not completely wrong.’","A faint smile unconsciously appeared on her lips.","’I really do... miss Noah.’","While Arisha and Emma with her friends fighting and exploring in dungeon.","Somewhere far to the west of the Empire, a young man found himself facing an unknown danger.","His face was filled with fear and anxiety as he wondered how he had ended up in such a perilous situation.","It seemed his vacation was not going to be normal after all.","He was none other than Kaelan Nightfall.","----","[A/N: Hello, guys!!","I hope you don’t mind that I’m showing the perspectives of other characters. They’re important to the story, and I want you to see what they’re doing during this time and what some of them are about to face.","Don’t worry! we’ll be back to Damien and Noah in another 2–3 Chapters!","Lastly, I hope you’ll keep sending me your Power Stones! The novel has been doing well this month. It’s not a huge jump, but it’s definitely improving, and I’m really grateful for your support.","I’m also slowly working on my third novel, but I’ll probably release it in November or December. Or maybe earlier. For now, I want to focus on my current two novels and make them as good as possible.","Anyways, bye!!]"]},{"number":232,"title":"Chapter 232: Shadow [1]","paragraphs":["Meanwhile...Duchy of Ebonreach. Also known as the Duchy of Nightfall.","Situated on the western frontier of the Aurelian Empire, the Duchy of Ebonreach had been ruled by House Nightfall for centuries.","It was a land renowned for its disciplined knights, intelligence network, and unwavering loyalty to the Empire.","At the heart of the duchy stood Silverbrook City, the residence of the Nightfall family.","Currently... Kaelan Nightfall was effectively under house arrest.","Not because he had committed any crime. But for his own safety.","During the practical examination at Novaris Academy, demons had infiltrated the testing grounds with a single objective.","To assassinate Kaelan Nightfall.","Since that incident, security around the young heir had become stricter than ever. Elite knights patrolled the estate day and night.","Magic barriers surrounded the mansion. Every servant entering or leaving underwent inspection.","Kaelan wasn’t even allowed to leave the estate grounds.","\"Haa...\"","Kaelan wiped the sweat from his forehead with a towel after finishing another exhausting training session.","\"I really feel like I’m living inside a prison.\"","His complaint echoed throughout the spacious training hall.","Standing nearby was a man in his early thirties.","He wore simple training clothes instead of armor, yet his muscular physique and composed posture immediately revealed that he was no ordinary knight.","He was Drake Steelborn.","Captain of the Nightfall Knights and currently...","Kaelan’s personal bodyguard.","Drake smiled helplessly.","\"Young Master... Everything we’re doing is for your safety. I know.\"","Kaelan sighed. \"I understand why Father made this decision.\"","He tossed the towel toward a waiting servant before walking out of the training hall. \"But that doesn’t change the fact that I can’t leave the estate.\"","Drake quietly followed behind him. His current mission was simple. Protect Kaelan at all costs during the summer vacation.","The two walked through the long stone corridors of the mansion. After several minutes of silence, Kaelan spoke again.","\"By the way... Has Father returned yet?\"","Drake shook his head.","\"Not yet. He’s still investigating your uncle’s whereabouts. Cassian Nightfall.\"","Kaelan’s expression immediately became serious.","\"Any progress?\"","Drake nodded.","\"We recently received intelligence suggesting Lord Cassian was seen in the eastern dukedom Raigamine. The territory ruled by House Narukami.\"","Kaelan stopped walking.","\"...Really?\"","His eyes widened in surprise.","\"How? He disappeared years ago. No matter how much we searched, we never found a single clue. So how did Father suddenly obtain information about him?\"","A faint smile appeared on Drake’s face.","\"Young Master... There are eyes everywhere throughout the Empire. Countless people make their living gathering and selling information. They trade secrets to noble families, merchants, and even governments.\"","Kaelan looked thoughtful.","\"You mean... An underground intelligence organization?\"","Drake nodded.","\"Something like that.\"","\"What are they called?\" Kaelan asked.","Drake gave an apologetic smile.","\"I’m afraid I don’t know. Only your father deals with them directly.\"","Kaelan studied Drake’s face carefully.","For just a brief moment. He felt Drake wasn’t telling him the whole truth.","But he chose not to pursue the matter further. If Drake wished to keep it secret.","There was probably a reason. By the time they returned to the residential wing...","The sun had already begun setting beyond the western mountains. The sky glowed with shades of crimson and orange.","\"I’ll freshen up.\"","Kaelan stopped outside his bedroom. \"Please have dinner sent to my room.\"","Drake bowed respectfully. \"As you wish, Young Master.\"","The knight turned and walked away. Kaelan entered his spacious chamber before heading directly toward the bathroom.","After a relaxing bath. He changed into comfortable clothes. Not long afterward, servants delivered his dinner.","The meal passed quietly. Night had completely fallen. The moon hung high above the sky.","Its silver light illuminated the estate gardens beyond the enormous bedroom window.","Kaelan slowly approached the glass. Looking outside he couldn’t help admiring the peaceful scenery.","The moonlight reflected across the fountains and flower gardens, creating an almost dreamlike landscape.","\"It’s beautiful, isn’t it?\"","A calm male voice suddenly spoke.","\"I mean... The moon. Oh also that moon is mine.\"","Without thinking, Kaelan answered.","\"Yeah...It really is. But how can be it you-\"","Then he froze. His pupils contracted. A chill ran down his spine. That voice it hadn’t come from outside. It had come from inside his room.","Almost instinctively, Kaelan summoned a pair of twin daggers from the storage ring on his finger. The weapons instantly appeared in his hands.","He spun around.","His sharp gray eyes scanned every corner of the chamber. \"...Who’s there?\"","There was only silence. Nothing other than silence.","No one was there.","\"Oh my~\"","The same male voice echoed again.","\"Why are you so tense? I’m not here to hurt you.\"","Kaelan’s heartbeat accelerated. His grip tightened around the daggers. He couldn’t see anyone.","He checked each corner of the chamber. No one was present. Yet someone was definitely inside the room.","Mana immediately surged through his body. He prepared to shout for help. How had anyone entered?","The Nightfall Estate was protected by countless elite knights and multiple layers of magical barriers. It should have been impossible.","\"Don’t shout, young man.\"","This time the voice came from directly behind him.","Kaelan instinctively turned. The instant he moved—","Darkness erupted from beneath his own shadow. Shadowy hands burst from the floor like living creatures.","Before he could react they wrapped around his arms.","His legs. His torso. Another hand covered his mouth.","Thud!","Kaelan lost his balance and fell heavily onto the floor. The living shadows completely restrained his body.","Only his frightened gray eyes remained visible.","Slowly he looked toward the window.","A lone figure stood there. Wrapped in a cloak darker than the night itself. The cloak seemed almost alive, blending perfectly with the surrounding darkness.","A simple black mask concealed his face. Only pitch-black eye sockets stared back at Kaelan.","His black hair gently swayed in the night breeze entering through the open window.","Most terrifying of all Kaelan couldn’t sense the slightest trace of mana.","There was no aura. There was no presence. It was as though the man standing before him didn’t exist.","Cold sweat rolled down Kaelan’s forehead. His heart pounded violently.","He wanted to ask who this person was. He wanted to scream. But the shadow covering his mouth prevented even the smallest sound from escaping.","The mysterious man spoke calmly.","\"Relax. I’m not here to kill you. If I wanted you dead... You would’ve died long before you realized I was in this room.\"","Those simple words made Kaelan’s blood run cold.","He knew the stranger wasn’t bluffing.","Someone capable of infiltrating the Nightfall Estate without alerting a single guard was unimaginably dangerous.","The masked man tilted his head thoughtfully.","\"So... How should I introduce myself?\"","He chuckled softly.","\"For now...You can call me...\" He pasued.","The said. \"...Shadow. Yes. Shadow.\"","He casually leaned against the window frame. \"I’m only here because there’s something important we need to discuss.\"","He glanced at the restrained young noble.","\"I’ll remove the shadow covering your mouth. But only if you promise not to scream.\"","Kaelan remained silent. His mind raced.","Calling for help would likely be pointless. If this man truly intended to kill him... No one in the estate would arrive in time.","After several tense moments. He slowly nodded.","Seeing that Shadow let out a low, eerie chuckle.","\"Hehehe~...Good.\"","The darkness covering Kaelan’s mouth slowly withdrew.","Shadow smiled beneath his mask.","\"Now then. Let’s talk. Kaelan Nightfall.\""]},{"number":233,"title":"Chapter 233: Shadow [2]","paragraphs":["Kaelan slowly sat down on the chair near the window.","Even though the shadow restraints had disappeared, he remained on guard. His twin daggers rested firmly in his hands, ready to strike at any moment.","The mysterious man continued leaning casually against the window, as if he were visiting an old friend rather than breaking into one of the most heavily guarded estates in the Empire.","Taking a deep breath to calm himself, Kaelan finally spoke.","\"...Who are you?\"","The masked man answered without hesitation.","\"Shadow.\"","Kaelan frowned.","\"I don’t mean your name. Who are you? Why are you here? And who sent you?\"","The man simply shrugged.","\"I already told you. I’m Shadow. No one send me. I came here on my accord. And I’m here because I have something very special to discuss with you.\"","Kaelan’s brows knitted together.","\"...Something special?\"","Shadow gave a mysterious chuckle.","\"You see... I’m Shadow. And I worship Death.\"","Silence filled the room.","Kaelan simply stared at him. He blinked once.","Then twice.","He patiently waited for the man to continue. Several seconds passed.","\"...What?\"","Shadow frowned behind his mask. \"Why aren’t you reacting?\"","He sounded genuinely confused. He had just revealed something monumental. He openly admitted to worshipping Death itself.","The young duke’s son should have been terrified. He should have looked horrified.","At the very least he should have shown some fear.","InsteaKaelan merely looked puzzled.","\"...Death?\"","After waiting for another explanation that never came, Kaelan cautiously asked,","\"Who is Death?\"","\"...\"","Shadow stood completely still.","Then, \"Dammit! You don’t know who Death is?! You fool!\"","His frustrated shout echoed throughout the room.","\"When I say Death... I mean Death. The God of Death!\"","Only then did Kaelan’s eyes widen in surprise.","Seeing that reaction...","Shadow finally felt a little satisfied.","There. That’s the expression he was expecting from Kaelan.","\"...The God of Death?\"","Kaelan frowned thoughtfully.","\"...This is actually the first time I’ve ever heard of such a god.\"","\"...Cough.\"","Shadow nearly choked.His shoulders twitched slightly beneath the cloak.","His god was completely unknown.","\"Damn this era...\"","He muttered under his breath.","Kaelan looked genuinely confused.","\"I’m serious. As far as I know... The only deity worshipped throughout the Human Empire is the Sun God. Even the elves offer prayers to Him.\"","Shadow suddenly laughed.","\"Haha... Of course they do. In this era... No one remembers Him anymore.\"","Kaelan tilted his head.","\"What do you mean? I’ve studied history since childhood. There has never been any mention of a God of Death. Not even in the oldest historical records.\"","Shadow quietly fell silent.","For the first time since entering the room...","He seemed lost in thought.","\"...Yeah. Maybe you’re right. Perhaps He wasn’t active back then...Or perhaps He couldn’t descend into this world. ...Or maybe... He simply hadn’t awakened yet.\"","A faint smile appeared beneath his mask.","\"But now... Our God is ready. He shall descend into this world.\"","Kaelan scratched his cheek awkwardly.","\"...Right. I think I understand...\"","To be honest...","The overwhelming fear Kaelan had initially felt was gradually disappearing. The mysterious intruder no longer seemed like an emotionless assassin.","If anything he behaved like an overly enthusiastic believer trying to recruit new followers.","Still Kaelan never relaxed his guard.","Anyone capable of infiltrating the Nightfall Estate unnoticed remained unimaginably dangerous.","\"So... What exactly does any of this have to do with me?\"","Shadow’s playful tone disappeared.","His voice became lower. It was cold and more serious.","\"You are a very fortunate young man.\"","Kaelan instinctively swallowed. The atmosphere inside the room immediately became heavier.","\"I’ve come here today...to offer you a proposal.\"","\"A proposal? What kind?\"","Shadow folded his arms. \"The greatest honor you’ll ever receive.\"","He spread his arms dramatically.","\"I’ve decided...to allow you to join my cult dedicated to the God of Death.\"","He pointed directly at Kaelan.","\"You’ll become the second-highest-ranking member. Right below me.\"","Silence.","Complete silence.","Kaelan stared at him as though wondering whether he had misheard.","He was the heir of House Nightfall. The future Duke of Ebonreach. And this mysterious man had just asked him...","To join an unknown cult devoted to a god no one had ever heard of.","Kaelan desperately wanted to tell him he had lost his mind.","Unfortunately he also wished to remain alive.","Maintaining a polite smile, he carefully replied,","\"Sir Shadow... I appreciate the offer. But may I ask something?\"","Shadow nodded.","\"Go ahead.\"","\"Why should I join your cult? I don’t believe in your god. I’ve never even heard of Him. And... I honestly don’t see anything that would persuade me to join.\"","\"Hmm...\"","Shadow rubbed his chin thoughtfully.","\"You have a point. There should be a compelling reason.\"","He began counting on his fingers.","\"You don’t have anyone you desperately want revenge against. So that motivation is out. You’re also talented. You aren’t some powerless nobody dreaming of becoming the strongest. So you have no reason to seek forbidden power.\"","He raised another finger.","\"You haven’t lost someone precious whom you’re desperately trying to bring back to life.\"","He let out a disappointed sigh.","\"...Sigh. You’re really not suitable for becoming the protagonist of a novel.\"","A vein bulged on Kaelan’s forehead. Out of everything that had happened tonight.","For some reason...","That comment irritated him the most.","’Why am I suddenly being judged as a novel protagonist...?’","Suppressing the urge to argue, Kaelan sighed.","\"...Exactly. So if I have no reason... Why do you want me in your cult? I hope you can just leave me alone... I will keep our meeting as a secret and forget about it like this all never happen.\"","Shadow smiled beneath his mask.","Then his next sentence erased every trace of humor.","\"...Don’t you want to know why the demons tried to assassinate you?\"","Kaelan froze.","His expression immediately changed.","\"...What? How... How do you know about that?\"","A quiet, eerie chuckle echoed through the room.","\"Hehehe... I know many things.\"","Shadow casually continued,","\"I even know where your uncle Cassian is.\"","Kaelan’s pupils contracted. His heartbeat quickened once more. His father had spent years searching for Cassian Nightfall.","Countless intelligence networks had failed. Yet this mysterious man spoke about it as though it were common knowledge.","At that moment. Kaelan realized something.","This wasn’t an ordinary cultist.","The man standing before him possessed information that even one of the Empire’s greatest ducal families couldn’t obtain. And he could also tell that the man name shadow was stronger than his own father.","And that made him far more dangerous than Kaelan had initially imagined."]},{"number":234,"title":"Chapter 234: Shadow [3]","paragraphs":["Kaelan stared at the masked man with narrowed eyes.","\"...You’re not bluffing, are you? You really have information about all of this?\"","Shadow nodded calmly.","\"I do. My organization doesn’t merely worship the God of Death. Our true objective something more than just praying, it is to bring peace to this world.\"","He folded his arms behind his back. \"For that purpose, we’ve built an extensive intelligence network. We gather information from every corner of the world. Only by understanding the dangers before they emerge can we hope to stop them before innocent people suffer.\"","Kaelan remained silent.","He carefully analyzed every word.","If... if this mysterious man was telling the truth. Then the organization behind him possessed an intelligence network capable of rivaling, or perhaps even surpassing, those of the Empire’s greatest noble families.","Still Kaelan couldn’t find a convincing reason to join him.","Yet his recent experiences made him hesitate.","First, the cultists in the forest near Okahaven had nearly sacrificed him alongside his classmates.","Then, during the academy’s practical examination. Demons had infiltrated the test solely to assassinate him.","His life had become one dangerous incident after another. If he could learn about such threats beforehand...","He could prepare for them. He could protect himself. And perhaps...Protect the people around him as well.","That thought alone was undeniably tempting.","Shadow watched Kaelan’s expression carefully.","Then he smiled beneath his mask. \"That’s not all. If you work with me... You’ll become much stronger.\"","He stepped closer. \"It’s time you stepped outside your comfort zone. Stop letting others make every decision for you. Choose your own future.\"","Kaelan frowned. \"...You’re far too suspicious. What makes you think I’d simply believe anything you say?\"","Shadow chuckled. \"Hehe... Because I’m not your enemy. Yes. I worship the God of Death. But that doesn’t mean I want everyone else to do the same.\"","He shook his head. \"I’m not asking you to become a believer. I’m simply inviting you to become part of my organization or my cult group.. whatever your like to call it..\"","Kaelan looked unconvinced. \"...Even so...Why me? I’m still weak. I’m just a student. Even if i am duke’s son there is hardly anything I can do, I don’t have huge influence like my father. So why would someone like you want me? And why offer me the second-highest position?\"","Shadow laughed softly. \"Because you’re special.\"","He looked directly into Kaelan’s gray eyes. \"The darkness you wield...isn’t ordinary. It wasn’t merely awakened by chance. It was bestowed upon you. By Death Himself. For He is also the ruler of darkness.\"","Kaelan’s pupils contracted. His mind was thrown into complete confusion. He wanted to dismiss everything as nonsense.","But he couldn’t ignore the strange certainty with which Shadow spoke.","Still he couldn’t simply trust a complete stranger.","His thoughts became increasingly chaotic.","’Should I pretend to accept...? Then tell Father everything afterward? No... What if he realizes I’m lying?Should I pretend to accept...? Then tell Father everything afterward? No... What if he realizes I’m lying?","’This man infiltrated the Nightfall Estate without a single guard noticing. Even Captain Drake, who’s only one rank below Father, sensed absolutely nothing.This man infiltrated the Nightfall Estate without a single guard noticing. Even Captain Drake, who’s only one rank below Father, sensed absolutely nothing.’","’If Shadow truly wanted to kill me...I’d already be dead.’ And he can do that in future as well.","’I don’t even know how he look like.’","Kaelan slowly exhaled. Then another question crossed his mind.","\"...Tell me. Where is my uncle? Where is Cassian Nightfall?\"","Shadow answered without the slightest hesitation.","\"Oh...He’s in the eastern duchy. Deep inside one of the great forests. He was there yesterday. Although... Knowing him... He’s probably already left.\"","Kaelan immediately focused on the details.","His father already knew Cassian had been seen somewhere within the Raigamine Duchy.","But no one knew his exact location. Not even Duke Nightfall. At least Kaelan thought so. That meant Shadow’s intelligence network was far superior to the one his father knew about.","While Kaelan was thinking, Shadow continued to talk.","\"...Why was he there? To retrieve a special scroll. One hidden inside an ancient abandoned shrine deep within the forest.\"","Kaelan’s heartbeat quickened.","That level of detail. Wasn’t something anyone could fabricate so casually.","He stared at Shadow.","\"...What’s the name of the forest? Aokamori Forest.\"","Shadow answered instantly.","\"There. Are you satisfied now?\"","\"...I...\"","Kaelan couldn’t immediately respond.","Silence filled the room.","Finally he asked the question that mattered most.","\"...Why did the demons try to kill me?\"","Shadow smiled.","\"I’ll gladly answer...After you join my organization.\"","Kaelan immediately replied,","\"I’ll join after you tell me.\"","Shadow shook his head.","\"No.\"","\"...Damn it.\"","Kaelan clicked his tongue in frustration. Both of them fell silent once again.","After thinking for nearly a full minute...","Kaelan finally spoke.","\"...I need time. I can’t make a decision tonight.\"","Shadow nodded surprisingly easily.","\"That’s fair. I’ll give you a few days.\"","He turned toward the window.","\"I’ll return afterward. I hope you’ll have a favorable answer.\"","\"...Wait.\"","Kaelan suddenly called out.","Shadow paused. \"One last question.\"","\"If I’m really that special... Why offer me the second-highest position? I’m still weak. I’ve accomplished nothing. So why place me above everyone else?\"","Shadow burst into laughter.","\"Hehehe...\"","\"Oh...The reason is actually very simple.\"","Kaelan waited.","Shadow casually answered,","\"Because... My organization currently has exactly one member...that is me.\"","Silence.","Absolute silence.","Kaelan simply stared. His mind completely stopped processing information.","All this time he had imagined some enormous secret organization hidden within the shadows of the world. Or some huge cultist group that madly worship their god.","Instead this mysterious cult consisted of one person.","Just Shadow.","Seeing Kaelan’s dumbfounded expression, Shadow laughed even harder.","\"So...I hope you’ll become my very first subordinate. My first official member.\"","Kaelan hurriedly stood.","\"W-Wait—\"","He reached out instinctively. But before another word could leave his mouth.","Shadow’s body dissolved into darkness. His figure melted into the shadow cast beneath his own feet.","Like ink sinking into black water. He disappeared completely. Not even a trace of mana remained.","The room became silent once more.","Kaelan stood frozen for several long seconds.","Then he slowly lowered his hand.","\"What...\"","He blinked repeatedly.","\"Was he seriously alone? So he isn’t the leader of some massive hidden organization. He’s just a complete beginner trying to start one?\"","For the first time that night Kaelan genuinely didn’t know whether to laugh or be even more worried."]},{"number":235,"title":"Chapter 235: Labyrinth [11]","paragraphs":["While everyone else was dealing with their own challenges and making steady progress.","Noah and Damien continued to encounter one life-threatening situation after another. The labyrinth seemed determined to test them at every turn.","Fourth Floor","After finally escaping the underground forest, the two arrived at the fourth floor.","The scenery changed completely once again.","Instead of forests or ancient ruins.","An enormous submerged city spread before them.","Countless stone buildings rested beneath crystal-clear water, their rooftops barely visible above the surface. Broken towers and collapsed bridges stretched into the distance, giving the impression that an entire civilization had once flourished here before being swallowed by the depths.","The water was surprisingly calm. But beneath its tranquil surface.","Danger lurked everywhere. Noah knew that there would be danger inside the water.","This floor was inhabited by aquatic monsters unlike anything Noah had ever fought before.","Giant serpentine fish. Razor-finned predators.","Massive crustaceans. And countless other creatures that attacked from beneath the water without warning.","Fortunately, the difficulty of the floor turned out to be much lower than they had initially expected.","Noah quickly came up with a simple strategy. He looked toward the endless expanse of water before speaking.","\"I’ll freeze a path across the water. We’ll run straight to the opposite side.\"","He glanced at Damien.","\"You focus on killing anything that tries to attack us.\"","Damien grinned confidently.","\"Got it, bro. Leave it to me.\"","Without wasting another second...","Noah slammed his hand onto the water’s surface.","Mana surged outward.","Crack...!","An enormous sheet of ice rapidly spread across the water, forming a sturdy frozen road stretching toward the distant ruins.","The two immediately sprinted forward. Whenever monsters burst from beneath the water...","Damien intercepted them.","Golden light exploded from his sword as one aquatic creature after another fell before they could even reach Noah.","Even so crossing the fourth floor proved far more troublesome than expected. Although the monsters themselves weren’t overwhelmingly powerful...","The floor was filled with hidden traps. Pressure plates concealed beneath the water. Poison dart mechanisms hidden inside ruined buildings.","Collapsing bridges. Explosive magical formations left behind by the ancient civilization.","Each trap slowed their progress. To make matters worse.","The entrance leading to the fifth floor had been cleverly concealed within last submerge building. It was good that Noah and Damien tried to find it from last building of the floor.","Still finding it alone consumed a considerable amount of time. By the time they finally located the hidden passage.","More than two days had passed.","Fifth Floor","After each floor they would come to a small chamber where there’s chest box. Sadly it was not present on each floor.","Then the moment they stepped onto the next floor. The atmosphere changed again. This time they found themselves inside a gigantic stone fortress.","Long corridors stretched endlessly in every direction. The walls were decorated with faded banners and rusted suits of armor.","An eerie silence filled the fortress.","At least until it was shattered.","\"Fuck!!\"","Noah and Damien sprinted through one of the massive corridors as fast as they could.","Behind them an entire undead legion gave chase. Dozens upon dozens of skeletal knights rushed after them.","Their empty eye sockets glowed with ghostly blue flames. Rusted swords scraped against the stone floor as they charged forward without fear or exhaustion.","The sound of countless armored footsteps echoed throughout the fortress.","\"Dammit! Why are there so many of them?!\"","Damien shouted while continuing to run.","Even Noah couldn’t help feeling overwhelmed.","\"There must be hundreds...\"","Just then an idea flashed through Noah’s mind.","His eyes widened.","\"Oi!\"","He turned toward Damien while still running.","\"You’re a Light Element user! You have a natural advantage against undead!\"","\"Use the special light mana attribute within your Solar Core!\"","Damien blinked.","Then realization struck him.","\"...Right.\"","His frightened expression instantly disappeared.","A confident grin spread across his face.","\"Haha... Let’s see how effective it really is.\"","He abruptly stopped running. Golden mana erupted from his body.","Brilliant sunlight illuminated the dark corridor.","The skeletons instinctively slowed. The divine energy radiating from Damien was something every undead creature instinctively feared.","His sword became enveloped in dazzling golden light.","Unlike ordinary Light produce by normal mana, this radiance carried a faint trace of divinity bestowed by his Solar Core.","The air itself seemed to tremble.","Damien smiled.","\"My turn.\"","He shot forward like a beam of sunlight.","BOOM!!","His sword swept across the battlefield. The first skeletal knight exploded into fragments the instant the divine blade touched it.","Golden light spread through the undead ranks.","One skeleton after another disintegrated into glowing particles.","Meanwhile Noah supported him from the rear.","Massive walls of ice erupted throughout the corridor, trapping groups of undead before freezing them solid.","Those who escaped were immediately crushed beneath countless ice spears. The battle quickly turned into a massacre.","The very enemies that had forced them to flee moments earlier now stood no chance against Damien’s overwhelming elemental advantage.","By the following day after fighting through countless undead patrols and navigating the labyrinthine fortress the two finally discovered an enormous stone door hidden behind the castle’s throne room.","Ancient runes glowed faintly across its weathered surface.","Beyond it awaited the sixth floor of the labyrinth.","---","\"This floor is going to be troublesome...\"","Damien muttered as he looked around cautiously.","Noah shrugged.","\"Honestly... I think it’s still easier than some of the previous floors.\"","BOOM!!","A suit of enchanted armor swung its massive sword downward.","Damien hurriedly raised his own blade to block it.","Clang!!","The collision echoed throughout the enormous chamber.","\"...How is this easier?!\" Damien shouted while struggling against the towering suit of armor.","Unlike ordinary monsters. These enemies weren’t living creatures.","They were nothing more than empty suits of knightly armor animated by ancient magic.","Only endless attacks. The room they had entered resembled an ancient library.","Towering bookshelves stretched toward the ceiling, packed with thousands upon thousands of books.","Dust covered nearly every shelf, giving the impression that no one had stepped inside for centuries. At the corners of the vast library stood dozens of suits of knight armor.","At first glance they appeared to be nothing more than decorations. But now when they were attacking. Noah and Damien got to know just how strong they were.","---","[A/N: Keke~ Now I will write faster. And save your time.]"]},{"number":236,"title":"Chapter 236: Labyrinth [12]","paragraphs":["Earlier, Noah and Damien had searched nearly every bookshelf, hoping to find a clue leading to the next floor.","Instead they discovered something far stranger.","Every single book was completely blank. Not a single word had been written inside them.","Just as they had begun wondering what kind of place this was, one book suddenly floated off its shelf.","It slowly drifted toward them before opening by itself. Its pages were blank for only a moment.","Then dark letters gradually appeared across the paper as though an invisible hand was writing them.","Noah quietly read the riddle aloud.","I consume forests, cities, and kings.I have no mouth, yet swallow all things. No sword can wound me, no chains can bind me.Those who ignore me will leave nothing behind.","The library fell silent.","Noah read it again. Then a third time. He carefully considered every line.","Meanwhile Damien confidently stepped forward.","\"I know this one.\"","He crossed his arms proudly.","\"...Sleep?\"","The instant the word left his mouth.","BOOM!!","One of the motionless suits of armor suddenly came to life. Its eyes glowed crimson.","Without warning, it charged straight toward Damien.","\"Oi! What the—?!\"","Clang!","Damien barely managed to block the first strike. The enchanted knight continued attacking relentlessly.","Seeing this, Noah pinched the bridge of his nose.","\"...Honestly.\"","He looked toward the floating book and calmly answered,","\"Time.\"","The moment the word echoed through the library. The armored knight abruptly froze.","Its sword stopped mere centimeters from Damien’s face.","A second later the magical light within its helmet disappeared.","The armor returned to its original position as though nothing had happened.","Damien let out a long sigh of relief before walking back toward Noah.","\"...You’re smarter.\"","He sheathed his sword. \"You handle the riddles. I’ll keep my mouth shut.\"","A faint smile appeared on Noah’s face.","\"That’s probably for the best.\"","Damien scratched the back of his head awkwardly.","\"...Yeah. I think so too.\"","---","After one week...","And one additional day.","A total of eight days had passed since Noah and Damien first entered the labyrinth.","At long last...","They arrived at the final floor.","Damien stretched his aching shoulders before letting out a long sigh.","\"Haa...\"","\"That was one hell of a journey.\"","Noah rolled his stiff neck and nodded.","\"It really was.\"","He recalled the countless battles they had fought over the past week.","The endless forest.","The submerged city.","The undead fortress.","The cursed library.","Every floor had tested them in a completely different way.","Damien chuckled.","\"Honestly...\"","\"That undead fortress was incredibly annoying.\"","Noah raised an eyebrow.","\"Annoying?\"","\"I thought that floor was easier than the library.\"","He looked at Damien with an amused smile.","\"You have no right to complain after getting attacked by enchanted armor every time you answered a riddle incorrectly.\"","Damien immediately frowned.","\"Don’t remind me.\"","\"My brain almost stopped working in that place.\"","\"I’d rather fight a hundred skeletons than answer another one of those ridiculous riddles.\"","Noah laughed softly.","\"Well...\"","\"That’s behind us now.\"","He looked ahead.","\"Let’s see what the final floor has prepared for us.\"","The two stepped forward. Unlike the previous floors this place resembled a gigantic underground cavern.","Countless enormous stone stalactites hung upside down from the ceiling like the fangs of some ancient beast.","The cavern was vast enough that its farthest walls disappeared into darkness.","Near the center stood an ancient ruin.","A solitary stone structure that had somehow survived the passage of countless centuries.","Rows of blue mana lanterns were embedded into the surrounding walls.","Their soft azure light illuminated the otherwise dark cavern, giving the entire place an eerie yet mysterious atmosphere.","Damien looked around cautiously.","\"...Now what exactly is this place?\"","Noah slowly drew his sword.","\"I don’t know. But let’s stay alert.\"","They carefully approached the ancient ruin.","Despite its incredible age the structure remained remarkably intact.","Not a single wall had collapsed. Not a single pillar leaned out of place. It was as though someone had preserved it perfectly.","The two climbed the worn stone staircase leading toward its entrance.","Click","Click","Their footsteps echoed softly against the ancient stone.","Eventually they entered the building. Beyond the entrance awaited a massive circular hall.","The room was supported by dozens of towering stone pillars arranged in a perfect ring.","The ceiling rose high above them, disappearing into darkness.","Near one side of the chamber stood two thick stone pillars.","Resting across them was a massive rectangular stone slab, almost resembling an altar.","Damien pointed toward it. \"What’s that?\"","Noah narrowed his eyes. \"...I don’t know. Let’s take a closer look.\"","Neither of them lowered their guard.","With swords firmly in hand they cautiously approached the stone slab.","When they finally reached it. Their eyes immediately focused on the carving engraved across its surface.","Noah frowned. \"...A dragon.\"","Once again they had encountered the image of a dragon.","Ever since entering the labyrinth.","Every door leading to the next floor had been decorated with the carving of an enormous black dragon whose eyes were inlaid with crimson gemstones.","This carving, however was different.","It wasn’t black. Nor did it possess gemstone eyes.","Everything had been carved from ordinary gray stone.","Even the dragon’s appearance differed slightly from the previous ones.","Its posture. Its wings. Even the shape of its horns. Everything seemed subtly different.","Damien folded his arms.","\"So what exactly are we supposed to do now?\"","He looked around the empty chamber.","\"There’s nothing here. Maybe we’re supposed to find a hidden passage?\"","Noah slowly turned around, carefully studying the entire hall. Stone pillars formed a perfect circle around the room.","The walls appeared completely solid.bThere were no visible doors.","There were no staircases nor obvious mechanisms. After several moments of observation, he nodded.","\"...Yeah. Let’s search everything. There has to be something hidden.\"","Damien grinned.","\"Sounds good.\"","The two immediately split up. They carefully examined every section of the circular chamber.","Their hands moved across the ancient walls. They pressed suspicious-looking stones.","Inspected the pillars for hidden runes. Checked the floor for pressure plates.","Every possibility was investigated. Several minutes passed.","Nothing happened.","Thud!","A dull mechanical sound echoed throughout the hall.","Noah instantly turned.","\"Damien?\"","From the opposite side of the chamber...","Damien raised one hand.","A single stone brick beneath his palm had sunk inward.","\"Noah! I think I found something!\"","Noah immediately tightened his grip around his sword.","\"Stay on guard! It could just as easily be a trap!\"","Damien nodded.","\"Already am.\"","The entire chamber suddenly began to tremble.","Rumble","Dust fell from the ceiling.","Then one section of the circular wall slowly slid open.","Thud!","A hidden passage revealed itself. Both young men instinctively raised their weapons.","Their eyes remained fixed on the darkness beyond the opening.","Something enormous began emerging from within. Heavy footsteps echoed through the passage.","Thud","Thud","Thud","As the figure finally stepped into the lantern light.","Noah smirked helplessly.","\"...Here we go again.\""]},{"number":237,"title":"Chapter 237: Labyrinth [13]","paragraphs":["THUD!","A deafening impact echoed throughout the circular hall. The stone floor trembled violently.","Both Noah and Damien instinctively tightened their grips on their swords as they stared at the hidden passage.","Something was coming from there. Another heavy step followed.","THUD!","A massive silhouette slowly emerged from the darkness.","\"...What the...\"","Noah’s voice trailed off.","For the first time since entering the labyrinth. He genuinely didn’t know what he was looking at.","The creature was enormous. Nearly ten meters tall.","Its entire body was covered in smooth, pitch-black skin that reflected almost no light, making it appear as though it had been sculpted from living darkness itself.","The dark blue dim light from lantern only made it look more dangerous.","Its proportions were disturbingly unnatural. Its arms hung so low that its elongated fingers nearly scraped against the ground.","Its legs were equally long, giving it an unnervingly thin yet towering frame. Its head was completely bald.","There were no ears.","No nose no visible mouth. At least until it slowly lifted its face.","In the center of its head a single enormous crimson eye stared silently into the room.","It blinked once. The scarlet iris glowed faintly in the darkness.","The creature showed no expression.","There was no anger nor excitement. It simply stood there silent and motionless. Like something that had just awakened from an unimaginably long slumber.","Its very existence filled the chamber with an oppressive atmosphere. Even the air itself seemed heavier.","THUD!","The giant took another step. The entire hall shook. Dust rained from the ceiling as tiny cracks spread across the stone floor beneath its foot.","Noah felt his heartbeat quicken.","’It’s powerful...’","That much was obvious. But that wasn’t what disturbed him. Something about this creature felt fundamentally different.","Every monster they had encountered so far possessed mana. Even the strongest among them radiated an identifiable presence.","This thing didn’t. Its existence felt strange.","Wrong.","As though it didn’t belong in this world. A cold chill crawled down Noah’s spine. The giant slowly turned its head. Its lone crimson eye settled upon Damien. For a brief moment there was silence.","Then its face split open. A gigantic mouth stretched across the lower half of its head, revealing countless jagged black teeth.","ROOOOOAAAAARRRRRRR!!","The roar exploded throughout the chamber. A visible shockwave erupted from its mouth.","BOOOOOOM!!","The violent air pressure swept across the hall like a hurricane.","Noah and Damien instinctively crossed their arms before their faces. Their feet slid several meters across the stone floor despite their efforts to remain standing.","The creature raised one enormous arm. Its gigantic palm descended toward Damien like a collapsing mountain.","\"...Shit!!\"","Golden mana erupted around Damien. His body flashed with brilliant light as he threw himself sideways.","The next instant.","BOOOOOOM!!!","The creature’s palm smashed into the exact spot where Damien had been standing only a heartbeat earlier. The entire hall shook violently.","Stone exploded into the air. A massive crater formed beneath the impact.","Without hesitation Noah counterattacked.","He dashed around the giant’s flank. Mana surged into his blade.","With one swift upward slash.","He used Ice Creation.","Crack!","Gigantic crystal-blue ice spikes burst violently from the ground. One after another. They surrounded the creature from every direction.","Each spike towered several meters high, forming a frozen prison around its massive body. The temperature throughout the hall plummeted instantly.","Cold frost rapidly climbed onto the giant’s legs. For a brief second the monster actually stopped moving.","Noah’s eyes lit up.","Then the giant casually shook one leg.","Crack","Fine fractures spread across every ice spike.","BOOM!!","The entire frozen prison shattered into thousands of glittering fragments.","\"...What?\"","Noah’s expression stiffened.","Meanwhile Damien had already begun casting another spell. Four brilliant golden magic circles materialized around the giant.","Golden chains forged from concentrated hot light shot outward simultaneously.","Clang!","Two wrapped tightly around its legs. The remaining two restrained both enormous arms. The divine chains glowed intensely as holy flames attempted to burn the creature’s dark skin.","Yet nothing happened. The flames couldn’t even leave scorch marks. The giant merely looked down at the restraints.","ROOOAAARRR!!","With overwhelming brute force it flexed its arms.","SNAP!","One chain broke. Then another.","Within seconds all four light restraints shattered like brittle glass. At the same time Noah raised both hands toward the sky. Nearly forty weapons of crystal ice rapidly materialized above the battlefield.","Swords.","Spears.","Lances.","This took slight toll on Noah’s brain. A small headache started. Each one shimmered beautifully beneath the blue glow of condensed mana.","\"...Go!\"","With a single command. Every weapon shot downward simultaneously.","Whoooosh!!","The barrage descended like a rain of frozen stars. The creature didn’t even attempt to dodge. The weapons struck its body one after another.","Clang!","Clang!","Clang!","The sound wasn’t flesh being pierced. It was metal striking an indestructible wall. Not a single weapon penetrated its skin. Most shattered on impact. The few that remained intact managed only to leave shallow scratches across its black flesh.","Nothing more.","\"...Damn it!\"","Noah’s eyes widened. Its durability far exceeded anything he had anticipated. The giant immediately charged toward him.","Despite its colossal size, it moved with terrifying speed.","Noah reacted instantly. He threw himself sideways.","BOOOOOOM!!!","The giant’s fist crashed into the ground where Noah had been standing only an instant earlier. The stone floor exploded beneath the impact.","Chunks of rock flew through the air. The shockwave alone sent Noah tumbling several meters across the chamber before he regained his footing.","Dust filled the hall. For the first time since entering the labyrinth... Both Noah and Damien realized the same thing.","This wasn’t an ordinary floor boss. It was a monster unlike anything they had faced before.","ROOOOOOAAAAARRRRRRR!!!","The giant’s roar became even more ferocious. The sound shook the entire chamber, causing dust and fragments of stone to rain from the ceiling.","Its single crimson eye burned with murderous intent.","Then it attacked.","BOOM!!","This time it was more aggressive.","BOOM!!","Its colossal fist slammed into the floor. The impact shattered the stone tiles and sent a violent shockwave racing across the hall.","Noah and Damien sprang away in opposite directions just before the blow landed. Neither of them had time to counterattack.","They could only evade. The creature gave them no breathing room. They didn’t get much chance to attack or conjure any magic spell.","BOOM!!","Its other fist crashed down immediately afterward. The floor exploded once again. Stone fragments shot through the air like deadly shrapnel.","Noah narrowly twisted his body, avoiding the fist by mere centimeters. The wind pressure alone threw him several meters across the ground.","\"...Damn!\"","Before he could regain his footing. The monster was already in front of him.","\"What?!\"","Its speed had increased dramatically. Despite its enormous size, it moved with terrifying agility.","It swung one massive arm horizontally.","Noah instinctively raised layers of ice walls between them.","CRASH!!","The walls shattered instantly.","The attack continued without losing momentum.","Noah crossed his sword in front of his body.","BOOM!!","The impact struck like a speeding boulder. His entire body was launched through the air.","Crack!","A sharp pain exploded through his chest.","Several ribs fractured at once.","\"Urgh...!\"","Blood spilled from Noah’s mouth as he crashed across the stone floor, tumbling repeatedly before finally coming to a stop against one of the massive pillars.","His vision blurred. Every breath sent unbearable pain through his chest.","Meanwhile Damien wasn’t faring any better.","Golden mana erupted around him as he continuously unleashed radiant sword strikes, trying to keep the monster occupied.","[Heavenly Sacred Radiance]","\"Haaah!\"","His blade flashed repeatedly. Brilliant arcs of light slammed into the creature’s body.","Yet they barely left more than shallow cuts.The giant didn’t even slow down.","It simply raised one enormous hand.","Damien’s eyes widened. It was too fast.","He couldn’t dodge in time.","BOOOOOOM!!","The gigantic backhand struck him squarely across the chest.","\"...Gah!\"","The world spun. Damien was sent flying like a broken doll. His body crashed through stone pillar before colliding violently against the far wall.","BOOM!!","The impact echoed throughout the chamber. He slid downward. Landing heavily upon the ancient stone slab engraved with the dragon.","For several seconds, he couldn’t move. Blood slowly seeped through his torn clothes, staining both his armor and the weathered stone beneath him.","His breathing became ragged.","\"...Cough...\"","A mouthful of blood spilled onto the dragon carving.","The giant slowly turned toward him. Its heavy footsteps echoed through the silent hall.","THUD","THUD","THUD","Each step felt like a hammer striking the ground.","Damien struggled to stand. His arms trembled. His body refused to obey him.","The creature reached him within moments.","Its enormous hand descended.","Before Damien could react. The giant wrapped its massive fingers around his body.","\"...Damn...!\"","He struggled desperately. Golden mana erupted from him. He slashed repeatedly at the creature’s fingers.","Clang!","Clang!","The attacks accomplished almost nothing. Its grip didn’t loosen even slightly.","Slowly almost leisurely the monster lifted Damien into the air. Its gigantic mouth gradually opened. Rows of jagged black teeth glistened in the blue lantern light. It intended to swallow him whole.","\"No! Dammit!\" Damien struggled but his body was too weak."]},{"number":238,"title":"Chapter 238: Labyrinth [14]","paragraphs":["\"No...!\"","Noah forced himself onto one knee. He was tired. Every movement sent agonizing pain through his broken ribs.","Blood continued dripping from the corner of his mouth. His vision blurred. But he ignored it. His eyes locked onto the monster.","’ I won’t let it eat Damien..’","Cold mana surged wildly around him. Above the creature’s head. A single sword of crystal ice silently formed.","Unlike his previous attacks. This blade contained nearly every ounce of mana he could gather in such a short moment.","It hovered silently for the briefest instant.","Shoot!!","SWIIIISSHHH!!","The ice sword became a streak of blue light. Its speed far exceeded every previous attack Noah had launched.","The giant noticed it but too late.","SHRRRK!!","The blade pierced directly into its lone crimson eye. For the first time the monster was wounded. Its crimson eye burst apart as dark blood sprayed through the air.","ROOOOOOOOOAAAAARRRRRRRRRRR!!!!","An ear-splitting scream erupted from the giant. It staggered backward violently.","Its enormous hand instinctively opened. Damien slipped free and was thrown several meters before crashing painfully across the stone floor.","Dark blood streamed endlessly from the ruined eye socket. The giant clutched its face with one hand while roaring in agony.","Its cries echoed throughout the entire cavern. The walls trembled. The ceiling shook.","Even the air itself seemed to vibrate beneath its furious screams.","A chill ran down both Noah’s and Damien’s spines. Despite the wound neither of them felt relief.","Instead an overwhelming sense of dread settled over them. Because they both realized the same terrifying truth.","They had only managed to blind it. They hadn’t come anywhere close to killing it.","The giant remained bent over, clutching its ruined eye. Its enormous body trembled violently as dark blood poured relentlessly through the gaps between its fingers.","The entire hall echoed with its agonized growls. This was their only opportunity.","Noah forced himself to move.","Every step sent unbearable pain through his fractured ribs, but he gritted his teeth and dragged his battered body across the shattered floor toward Damien.","Blood continued dripping from the corner of his mouth. When he finally reached Damien, he immediately reached into his storage ring.","Two healing potions. Two mana recovery potions.","Without wasting a second, he tossed one of each to Damien before uncorking his own bottles. They drank them one after another.","Warm energy spread throughout Noah’s battered body. The sharp pain in his ribs eased slightly.","His exhausted mana core also began recovering, though nowhere near enough for another prolonged battle.","Across from him, Damien leaned heavily against one of the stone pillars while drinking his own potions.","His breathing gradually became steadier.","Noah looked toward him. \"...Damien.\"","Damien raised his head. \"Use the emergency device Instructor Morgana gave us.\"","His voice was grave.","\"send her signal. This monster is beyond anything we’ve fought before. I don’t think we can defeat it on our own.\"","Damien silently looked toward the giant, which was still writhing in pain.","After a brief hesitation he nodded.","\"...Yeah.\"","He reached into his storage ring. A dark-purple crystal appeared in his hand. In the event of a life-threatening situation. All they had to do was inject mana into it.","The crystal would instantly transmit a distress signal to the instructors outside the labyrinth.","Damien poured his mana into it. The crystal glowed faintly.","He frowned. \"...That’s strange.\"","He tried again. Still nothing happened. A minute passed. Then another.","Noah’s expression slowly darkened. A growing sense of unease settled inside him.","\"...What are you doing? You only need to activate it. It should automatically send the signal to Instructor Morgana.\"","Damien’s face became increasingly grim.","\"I know. I’ve activated it few times before.\"","He looked at the silent crystal in disbelief. \"But... For some reason... It’s not working today.\"","Noah’s pupils contracted.","\"...What?...Fuck.\"","His heartbeat quickened.","’Why...? Did the labyrinth block it? No... that’s not possible. The instructor personally inspected this labyrinth before allowing Damien and me to enter. She gave us this device because she knew it would work... then why isn’t it working now? Or... is someone preventing it from transmitting?’","Before either of them could speak again. A deep, thunderous voice echoed throughout the chamber.","\"VENGEANCE.\"","The words reverberated through the ancient hall like the tolling of a massive bell.","Noah and Damien froze. Neither of them moved. Neither of them breathed. Slowly both turned toward the source of the voice.","The giant still stood with its back facing them. Its massive hand remained pressed against its ruined eye.","Damien instinctively gripped his sword tighter. His voice trembled.","\"D-Did...Did that thing just... speak?\"","Noah swallowed hard.","\"...Yes.\"","Silence returned. Then the giant spoke again.","Its voice was heavy.","Slow.","As though every word had been forgotten over countless centuries and had to be painfully remembered.","\"VENGEANCE...\"","A brief pause followed.","\"VENGEANCE!!!\"","Its tone grew louder. Filled with confusion. Almost as though it were recalling an old lesson.","Finally the creature spoke once more. Its words echoed throughout the chamber.","\"PUNISHING...\"","\"AND HARMING SOMEONE...\"","\"IN RETURN...\"","\"FOR SOMETHING BAD THEY HAVE DONE TO YOU.\"","Each sentence came slowly.","Broken.","Like fragments of memories buried deep within its mind.","Then it finished.","\"THAT... IS WHAT FATHER SAID.\"","The giant slowly lowered its hand. It turned around. Black blood continued streaming from the ruined eye socket, running down its face and dripping onto the shattered floor.","Its breathing had become heavier.","More violent. It glared directly at Noah and Damien.","A low growl escaped its throat, one filled not merely with rage, but with grief and with resentment. Full of hatred for both humans.","And with an endless hatred that had survived for countless years.","For the first time neither Noah nor Damien saw it as a mindless monster.","Something about those broken words made it sound terrifyingly human. Or perhaps it was something else entirely.","But one thing was sure. Both Noah and Damien have to give their all to kill this creature."]},{"number":239,"title":"Chapter 239: Labyrinth [15]","paragraphs":["\"Noah...\"","Damien’s voice was unusually tense.","\"...Do you remember the monster we fought in the dungeon? The one that suddenly started speaking?\"","Noah never took his eyes off the giant. He gave a slow nod.","\"...I remember.\"","His grip tightened around his sword.","\"But that creature was different. It was being controlled by someone.\"","He narrowed his frost-blue eyes.","\"This one isn’t. It isn’t under anyone’s control... And yet it can speak.\"","Damien swallowed. A chill ran down his spine.","The creature before them was unlike anything they had ever encountered.","It possessed intelligence. Fragments of memories.","And emotions. That alone made it far more terrifying than an ordinary monster.","Damien slowly rose to his feet despite the pain coursing through his battered body.","Golden mana began gathering around him.","\"...I’m using the full power of my Solar Core. If we’re going to survive...We have to go all out.\"","Noah nodded without hesitation. \"Yeah.\"","A thin layer of crystal-blue frost spread across the edge of his sword. Cold air rippled outward.","This battle would decide whether they lived or died.","The giant suddenly lifted its head.","ROOOOOAAARRR!!","The monstrous roar shook the entire fortress.","Then it charged. The enormous body moved with terrifying speed.","Stone shattered beneath every step.","Noah reacted first. He slammed his foot onto the ground.","He used Ice Creation","CRACK!!","A gigantic pillar of razor-sharp ice erupted from beneath the monster’s foot. The spike shot upward like a spear.","SHRK!","The point pierced into the sole of the giant’s foot. Dark blood sprayed across the frozen crystal.","\"...GRAAAAHHH!!\"","The monster let out a furious roar.","However the wound was nowhere near deep enough. With overwhelming strength, it simply forced its foot downward.","CRACK!!","The massive ice pillar fractured.","BOOM!!","It shattered into countless pieces.","Without stopping another gigantic ice pillar erupted directly in front of the giant.","The creature answered with pure brute force. It slammed both enormous fists downward.","BOOM!!","BOOM!!","BOOM!!","The pillar exploded apart.","Thousands of ice fragments were blasted high into the air before beginning to rain down throughout the chamber like a deadly hailstorm.","Amid the falling ice two streaks of light shot forward.","One was blue.","Other was golden.","Noah moved like flowing frost.","Damien became a blazing ray of sunlight.","They weaved effortlessly through the deadly rain of ice while charging straight toward the giant.","Golden and blue mana erupted simultaneously.","Noah swung his sword.","[Still Surface Cut]","A nearly invisible crescent of frozen mana silently sliced through the air.","At the same time Damien unleashed a barrage of radiant sword slashes.","Golden arcs crossed the battlefield one after another.","The giant crossed its arms instinctively. Even though it couldn’t see it could sense it.The attacks struck almost simultaneously.","Small cuts appeared across its body. Not deep but enough to force it backward.","Noah immediately continued his assault.","A massive greatsword of solid ice rapidly materialized beside the monster. Rather than throwing it. He leaped onto its broad, flat blade.","The enormous weapon floated through the air beneath his control.","It was the first time Noah had attempted such a technique during combat. Maintaining his balance proved far more difficult than expected.","The sword wobbled beneath his feet.","Still he pushed forward.","As the floating blade carried him beside the giant’s shoulder.","Noah jumped. He landed directly upon the creature’s massive shoulder.","With every ounce of strength remaining in his battered body. He swung his sword toward its neck.","CLANG!","The blade barely cut through the skin. Only a shallow wound appeared.","\"What?!\"","The giant roared in fury. Its enormous hand immediately reached toward its shoulder.","Noah didn’t hesitate. He kicked off the creature’s body.","Landing upon the stone floor, he rolled several times before regaining his footing.","Meanwhile Damien slipped beneath the gap between the monster’s legs.","Thanks to the destruction of its only eye. The giant had completely lost its vision.","Now it swung its arms wildly in every direction, relying solely on instinct and sound.","That blindness created the opening they desperately needed.","Noah’s frost-blue eyes glowed brilliantly as he went in front of monster. He stood meters away from it.","Beautiful trails of icy light followed every movement he made.","He raised one hand. All around the battlefield. The countless shards of shattered ice suddenly stopped falling.","For a single moment. It was as if time itself had frozen.","Then the fragments trembled.","One after another, every shard rose into the air. Hundreds of glittering crystals floated around Noah.","Responding to his will. They rapidly converged before him.","The countless pieces merged together.","They compressed. They condensed. And then refined.","Gradually an enormous lance of crystal ice took shape. It was nearly eight meters in length.","It was far denser than any weapon Noah had created before.","Its tip gleamed with frightening sharpness.","Then the lance began to spin. Slowly at first then faster.","Faster. Until it became nothing more than a blue blur. The rotation generated a violent vortex.","Winds howled around the weapon.","Remaining ice fragments were swept into the spiraling current, circling the lance like a frozen storm.","The amount of mana Noah poured into it was absurd. His veins bulged beneath his skin. Blood trickled from the corners of his eyes.","\"...Cough!\"","He spat another mouthful of blood.","Yet he refused to stop.","On the opposite side Damien had already reached the monster’s back.","He bent his knees. Golden mana exploded beneath his feet.","BOOM!!","He launched himself high into the air. Landing perfectly atop the giant’s shoulder.","The monster continued swinging blindly, unable to locate either of them.","Damien slowly raised his sword. His golden eyes shone with blinding brilliance.","The light surrounding him grew hotter.","Brighter.","More intense.","Then a miniature sun began to form from within him.","A sphere of condensed solar mana.","Radiating divine heat. It expanded rapidly.","The temperature throughout the hall soared.","Even the surrounding stone started glowing from the intense heat.","The blazing sun grew larger still. Until it completely engulfed the giant’s upper body.","GRAAAAAAAAHHHHHH!!","For the second time. The creature truly screamed in agony. But it was more painful than the last scream, when it’s eye was injured.","Its black skin began burning. Smoke poured from its body. Dark flesh charred beneath the divine flames.","The entire chamber became as bright as daylight. Watching the blazing sun from across the battlefield.","Noah smiled faintly despite the blood covering his face.","\"Good job...Damien.\"","He poured the last of his remaining mana into the spinning lance. The frozen weapon screamed through the air as the surrounding vortex intensified.","Finally the miniature sun faded.","Its energy exhausted.","Damien immediately jumped from the monster’s shoulder before the remaining flames consumed him as well.","He landed heavily upon the ground.","Panting and completely drained.","The giant still stood. Half of its upper body had been burned black.","Smoke continued rising from the charred flesh. Its breathing became heavy.","It was labored, weak and yet it remained standing.","The monster opened its mouth.","One final roar escaped.","ROOOOOOOOOAAARRRRRRRRR!!","Noah’s eyes sharpened.","\"...Now.\"","He thrust his hand forward. The enormous ice lance vanished.","No. It accelerated so quickly that it became invisible. A blue flash crossed the battlefield.","SHRRRRRK!!","The spinning lance pierced directly through the giant’s chest.","Its rotation drilled effortlessly through burned flesh, muscle, and bone before bursting out from its back.","A massive hole remained where its heart should have been.","The lance continued flying.","BOOOOOOM!!","It slammed into the far wall of the chamber, exploding with enough force to shake the entire ruin.","The giant remained motionless.","Still standing. For several long seconds. Neither Noah nor Damien breathed.","Then its colossal body slowly leaned backward.","THUD!!","The giant crashed onto the stone floor. The impact shook the entire hall. Dark blood poured endlessly from the gaping hole in its chest.","Silence finally descended upon the ancient ruin. After a battle that had pushed both of them to their absolute limits.","The creature who looked like the guardian of the final floor had fallen."]},{"number":240,"title":"Chapter 240: Labyrinth [16]","paragraphs":["Silence descended upon the ancient chamber.","The deafening roars.The explosions. The endless clash of steel and magic.","Everything had finally come to an end.","Only the ragged breathing of two exhausted young men echoed through the ruined hall.","Damien lay motionless in the middle of the battlefield, only a short distance away from the giant’s colossal corpse.","His chest rose and fell heavily as he stared blankly at the ceiling.","He didn’t even have the strength to sit up. On the opposite side of the chamber.","Noah staggered backward. His legs finally gave out.","His back struck the cold stone wall before he slowly slid down until he was sitting on the floor.","He leaned against the wall, breathing heavily. Every muscle in his body screamed in pain.","His vision blurred. His eyelids felt unbearably heavy.","\"...Cough...\"","A mouthful of blood spilled from his lips.","’I...I think I still have a few potions left.’","With trembling hands, Noah reached into his storage ring.","After fumbling for several seconds, he finally pulled out a healing potion and a mana recovery potion.","He uncorked both bottles with great difficulty. Then drank them one after another.","Warmth slowly spread throughout his battered body.","The fractured bones began knitting together at a painfully slow pace.","His torn muscles gradually recovered.","Meanwhile, the exhausted mana core within his body also started replenishing itself little by little.","It wasn’t nearly enough to restore him to full strength.","But at least it kept him conscious. Neither of them spoke for several minutes.","They simply rested.","Trying to recover enough strength to leave the labyrinth.","Eventually Damien let out a weak laugh.","\"We...We actually did it, Noah.\"","A small smile appeared on his bloodstained face.","\"We won.\"","Noah looked toward him.","Despite his exhaustion...","He smiled faintly and nodded.","\"...Yeah. We did.\"","His breathing remained uneven.","\"Let’s just...rest for a while.\"","Damien silently agreed.","The two closed their eyes for a brief moment.","Then","Tremble","A faint vibration spread through the chamber.","Noah’s eyes immediately opened. \"Hm?\"","Another vibration followed.","Tremble","He frowned. Something’s moving. He slowly turned his head toward the source of the sound.","His eyes settled upon the ancient stone slab engraved with the dragon.","It was trembling.","\"Dammit. What now?\"","Noah forced himself onto his feet. His entire body protested in agony.","Still he ignored the pain.","\"Damien.\"","His voice became serious.","\"I don’t think this is over. Get up.\"","Damien immediately opened his eyes.","Without asking any questions, he pushed himself upright, using his sword as support.","Meanwhile Noah cautiously approached the stone slab. An ice spear materialized within his hand.","He remained alert. Ready for anything.","His eyes narrowed. The dragon engraving had been stained with blood during the battle.","It belonged to Damien.","Now something unbelievable was happening. The blood covering the carving slowly began glowing.","Golden light spread across every crimson stain. Even the blood started to turn into golden color.","The glow became brighter with each passing second.","\"...What?\"","Noah whispered.","At the same moment. The towering stone pillars surrounding the circular hall began trembling violently.","Ancient runes hidden across their surfaces suddenly illuminated. Dark-blue mana pulsed through every pillar.","The entire ruin shook.","Damien, still leaning against his sword, slowly looked around.","\"What... is happening?\"","Noah didn’t answer.","Because he didn’t know. His grip around the ice spear tightened.","His heartbeat accelerated.","An uneasy feeling settled deep within his chest. Then the glowing pillars erupted.","Streams of dense blue mana burst from every pillar simultaneously.","Like rivers of light they converged toward the dragon-carved stone slab.","Noah instinctively stepped backward.","His eyes never left the altar.","There was fear, curiosity and confusion.","All three emotions mixed together. He suddenly turned toward Damien.","\"Damien! Get out of the hall!\"","Damien looked surprised. But seeing Noah’s serious expression.","He didn’t question him. He immediately turned toward the entrance of the ancient ruin.","Using his sword as support, he forced his exhausted legs to move.","Noah prepared to retreat as well.","Then space itself distorted.","A gigantic circular portal suddenly materialized above the stone slab.","Its interior was dark blue and black color.","\"Fuck.\"","The instant it appeared a terrifying suction force erupted from within.","WHOOOOSH!!","The violent pull swept across the chamber.","Broken stones.There was dust as well. Fragments of shattered ice.","Everything was dragged toward the portal.","\"No!\"","Noah slammed his spear into the ground, desperately trying to anchor himself.","His exhausted body trembled violently. He had almost no mana left.","His muscles were barely functioning. He simply didn’t possess the strength to resist.","His feet slowly slid across the floor.","\"...No...\"","\"No!\"","His fingers tightened around the spear. The stone beneath it cracked.","But it wasn’t enough.","The suction only grew stronger. Across the hall Damien turned around after hearing Noah’s desperate shout.","His eyes widened in horror.","\"Noah!\"","Ignoring his own injuries...","He sprinted back toward him.","Every step sent pain shooting through his battered body.","Still he kept running.","\"Noah!!\"","Their hands came within only a few meters of each other.","Then","WHOOSH!!","Noah was ripped from the ground.","His body disappeared into the black portal before Damien could reach him.","\"NOAH!!\"","Damien’s body also started to get suck. Using the force he lunged forward. His hand grasped nothing but empty air.","The portal flickered once. Then it vanished.","The chamber fell silent once more. The blue light faded. The pillars became lifeless stone again.","As though nothing had ever happened.","Damien stood frozen. His breathing became uneven.","\"Noah?\"","He stared at the empty space where his friend had disappeared.","No answer came.","Slowly he walked toward the stone slab.","The blood that had once stained the dragon carving had completely vanished.","Damien clenched his fists. His frustration boiled over.","\"Dammit!!\"","He slammed his fist against the stone slab.","BANG!!","Nothing happened. He struck it again.","\"Open!\"","Another punch.","\"Open, damn it!!\"","Again. And again.","But the ancient slob remained completely silent. Leaving Damien utterly alone inside the final chamber of the labyrinth.","\"Why? Dammit!!\"","He fell on his knees.","Damien didn’t know what just happened. Where did Noah went? Was that portal took him to another floor of labyrinth? Or to another"]},{"number":241,"title":"Chapter 241: What’s Happening?","paragraphs":["Damien continued pounding his fist against the ancient stone slab.","\"Open!\"","BANG!","\"Open, damn it!\"","The stone slab remained completely silent.","No matter how hard he struck it.","Nothing happened. His breathing became heavier. His frustration slowly turned into despair.","Where might be Noah? He was already too tired and I injured.","\"Dammit!!\"","Then a chill ran down his spine.","His instincts screamed. There was danger. Damien’s entire body froze.","He slowly turned around. And what he saw made his eyes immediately widened.","The giant’s corpse was moving.","\"...What?\"","The massive body lying across the chamber began to ripple unnaturally. Its black flesh undulated like the surface of disturbed water.","Something was moving beneath its skin.","It pushed outward from within, stretching the flesh into grotesque bulges before disappearing again.","Another bulge appeared. Then another appeared.","Whatever was inside was trying to get out.","Damien instinctively took several steps backward.","\"No...\"","The corpse convulsed violently. Every muscle twisted in impossible directions.","Dark blood seeped through newly formed cracks.","RIIIPPP!!","The giant’s upper body burst apart.","Black blood exploded throughout the chamber, splattering the pillars, walls, and floor.","Chunks of flesh scattered in every direction.","From the mangled corpse a hand emerged.","It was unnaturally pale. It was almost white. Its oily skin was coated in thick black blood that slowly dripped onto the stone floor.","The strange skin reflected the chamber’s dark-blue light in a way that felt profoundly wrong.","It was too smooth and too glossy. Almost as though it wasn’t skin at all. Long fingers gripped the torn flesh of the corpse.","Each finger ended in a long, curved black claw that scraped across the stone with an ear-piercing screech.","Green veins pulsed visibly beneath the pale skin. They spread like cracks through glass.","Slowly the creature pulled itself free.","First its shoulders. Then its chest. Then the rest of its grotesque body.","It stood nearly eight feet tall. At first glance its silhouette was vaguely humanoid.","It had two arms. And two legs. There was one head. But every other detail mocked the very idea of humanity.","Its proportions were disturbingly wrong. Its limbs were far too long. As it crawled free, it moved on all fours with unnatural flexibility before gradually straightening itself upright.","Damien saw its face.","His blood turned cold. Its mouth dominated nearly half its head. Far too wide. Far too large.","Rows upon rows of jagged teeth overlapped one another in impossible layers, as though countless mouths had been forced together into one.","Its eyes were enormous.","They were round and crimson.","They didn’t glow. Yet something deep within them burned with a cold, lifeless light.","Above the monstrous mouth. Two long black horns curved upward and outward.","Behind them. Five additional horns rose from the crown of its head like a twisted, demonic crown.","There was no nose. Only two narrow holes in the center of its face.","Each heavy breath caused them to flare open before closing again.","Its oily white skin covered its entire body.","Every movement reflected the surrounding light incorrectly, making it appear strangely unreal.","\"...No...\"","Damien whispered.","Recognition struck him like lightning.","\"I know you...\"","His pupils contracted.","’No... I have seen monster like it before... It’s...The same type of creature from the dungeon.’","It was the exact same creature. The same horrifying monster he and Noah had encountered during their dungeon exploration.","Only there was no one controlling this one. Before Damien could process the situation.","The wall beside him suddenly trembled.","Rumble a section of stone slowly slid aside.","Behind it a massive metal door was revealed. Ancient runes across its surface glowed with brilliant blue mana.","With a loud mechanical groan the door opened by itself.","Beyond it a passage bathed in bright azure light stretched into the distance.","It was almost as though the labyrinth had been waiting for this exact moment.","Damien didn’t hesitate. He turned and ran. Every step sent agony through his battered body.","His broken muscles screamed. His wounds reopened.","But he ignored everything. He sprinted toward the glowing passage.","Behind him the corpse split open again. Another pale hand emerged.","Then another. And another. The giant’s hollow body had become something else entirely.","As if it was a living portal. One after another. More of the white-skinned creatures crawled out from within its remains. Dozens.Then more.","It was as though an endless abyss existed inside the giant’s corpse.","The first creature slowly lifted its head. Its crimson eyes locked onto the escaping Damien.","It opened its grotesque mouth.","ROOOOOOAAARRRRRRR!!","Without warning it exploded forward. Its speed was terrifying.","The remaining creatures immediately followed. The entire swarm charged after Damien.","---","Meanwhile.","Far above the labyrinth...","At the same location where Damien and Noah had first entered the ancient ruins.","Where countless jagged rocks and massive boulders were scattered across the ground","Space suddenly distorted. A gigantic portal resembling a stone gate materialized in midair.","A moment later Damien was violently thrown out of it. He rolled across the rocky ground before crashing onto his knees.","Fresh blood spilled from his mouth.","He looked back. The portal behind him vanished almost instantly.","\"...Haa...\"","\"...Haa...\"","Ignoring the pain coursing through his body...","Damien forced himself to stand.","He had no time to rest.","He immediately pulled the dark-purple communication crystal from his storage ring.","With trembling hands...","He poured mana into it once again. This time the crystal lit up brilliantly. A pulse of purple light shot into the sky.","Damien’s exhausted face filled with relief.","\"It... worked...\"","He nearly collapsed from exhaustion.","\"Master...Please...Hurry...\"","He pushed himself up.","\"Noah... is he out as well? Did he come out?\" He looked around tired and run in random direction.","\"Noah!!\"","He screamed. He was trying to see if Noah was also here.","But just then from the portal opened in midair. Those creatures started to pour out.","Damien looked at them and cursed.","It was becoming total mess.","\"Noah is not here...then where did he go.\""]},{"number":242,"title":"Chapter 242: Monster Wave [1]","paragraphs":["Novaris City","On the eastern outskirts of Novaris City. The dungeon that Noah and Damien had explored remained under strict quarantine.","No civilians were allowed anywhere near it. Large transport vehicles belonging to the Hero Association surrounded the area.","Researchers carrying various magical instruments moved busily between temporary laboratories and observation tents, documenting every abnormal fluctuation coming from the dungeon.","Around them, dozens of adventurers stood guard with weapons in hand. A temporary camp had been established nearly a hundred meters away from the dungeon entrance.","The distance wasn’t chosen at random.","If the danger emerged from the dungeon.","The personnel would have enough time to retreat while the emergency defenses were activated.","---","Deep Inside the Dungeon","Far deep the surface. Hidden below one of the chamber.","Lay a gigantic natural cavern. Unlike the man-made looking above.","This place had been formed by nature itself.","Its walls were uneven. Jagged stone pillars stretched from floor to ceiling.","The cavern extended so far into the darkness that its end couldn’t even be seen.","Yet the most horrifying sight wasn’t the cavern itself.","It was what covered it.","Everywhere. Across the rocky floor.","Lining the walls even hanging motionless from sections of the cavern were creatures.","Hundreds of them.","Perhaps even thousands.","Every single one possessed the same horrifying appearance. Pale white skin with an oily sheen. Long unnaturally thin limbs.","Black curved claws. Green veins crawling beneath translucent flesh.","Massive mouths overflowing with jagged teeth. Seven black horns crowning their heads.","The exact same creatures Noah and Damien had encountered before.","The same monster Noah had killed inside the dungeon.","The same creatures that had crawled from the corpse of the giant guardian.","Every single one remained perfectly still.","They were like corpses or sleeping predators.","Silence ruled the cavern.","Then one finger twitched. A pale hand slowly clenched. Its enormous crimson eyes snapped open.","A cold red light illuminated the darkness. The creature slowly lifted its head.","Its chest expanded.","ROOOOOOAAARRRRRRR!!!","Its deafening roar echoed throughout the underground cavern.","The sound awakened everything. Hundreds of crimson eyes opened simultaneously.","---","Outside the Dungeon","Near the sealed entrance. Five adventurers stood watch.","A middle-aged swordsman named Gareth rested his weapon across his shoulder.","\"So...\"","He yawned.","\"Another quiet day.\"","Beside him, a young archer named Liana rolled her eyes.","\"You’ve said that every day this week. And every day you’ve nearly fallen asleep.\"","A muscular man carrying a battle axe laughed.","\"If monsters show up now, Gareth will probably die before drawing his sword.\"","\"Oh, shut up, Rowan.\"","A female mage adjusted her glasses.","\"I’d actually prefer another peaceful day. I’m tired of babysitting researchers.\"","The youngest among them, Theo, sighed.","\"I heard the Hero Association plans to keep this dungeon sealed for months. I don’t even know why we’re still guarding an empty cave.\"","Before anyone could answer...","Tremble...","The ground shook beneath their feet. Everyone instantly fell silent.","Gareth’s relaxed expression disappeared.","His sword was already in his hand.","\"...Did you feel that?\"","Another tremor followed.","Tremble...","Liana slowly aimed her bow toward the cave entrance.","\"...Something’s coming.\"","Rowan tightened his grip on his axe.","Theo’s face paled.","Gareth immediately shouted,","\"Battle positions!\"","All five adventurers instantly spread out into formation. Their eyes remained fixed upon the dark entrance.","The silence became suffocating.","A horrifying roar echoed from deep inside the dungeon.","ROOOOOAAARRRRR!!","Theo instinctively stepped backward.","\"...Captain...That didn’t sound like any monster I’ve ever heard.\"","Gareth’s expression became grim.","\"Forget identifying it.\"","He pointed toward the camp.","\"Theo!\"","\"Warn the Hero Association staff immediately! Tell them we have a possible dungeon outbreak!\"","Theo nodded without hesitation.","\"Yes, sir!\"","He immediately sprinted toward the research camp.","The remaining four tightened their formation.","Then something stepped out of the darkness.","A pale claw. A creature emerged. Its oily white skin reflected the sunlight unnaturally.","Its crimson eyes stared directly at them. Then another appeared.","Dozens came. Their horrifying roars echoed together.","ROOOOOAAARRRRRRR!!","Gareth’s face drained of color.","\"...Shit. There are too many!\"","The monsters didn’t stop.","They continued pouring from the dungeon entrance.","Hundreds of them. An endless tide of pale bodies.","Their mouths dripped saliva. Their crimson eyes burned with hunger.","Gareth immediately made his decision.","\"Fall back! Retreat to the defensive perimeter! Activate the emergency barrier!\"","The four adventurers immediately turned and ran.","Behind them the horde exploded forward. The creatures moved with terrifying speed. They closed the distance within seconds.","\"...They’re catching us!\"","Liana shouted.","A deafening scream suddenly echoed behind them.","\"AAAAAAAHHHHH!!\"","Theo who had been running toward the camp was the first to be caught.","One of the creatures leaped onto him. Its grotesque jaws opened impossibly wide.","CRUNCH!!","His head disappeared inside its mouth. Blood erupted across the ground.","His lifeless body collapsed without another sound.","\"...Theo!!\"","Rowan roared. His face twisted with rage. He suddenly stopped running.","Mana erupted around his body.","\"I’ll hold them back!\"","\"Go!\"","A massive crimson magic circle formed before him.","\"Flame Burst!\"","BOOOOOOM!!","An enormous explosion of fire engulfed the charging monsters.","Several were thrown backward.","Many burned. But it wasn’t enough. There were simply too many. The flames disappeared beneath the endless swarm.","\"...No—!\"","Within moments Rowan was overwhelmed. The creatures buried him beneath countless pale bodies.","His screams lasted only seconds. Gareth and Liana didn’t dare look back. They continued sprinting toward the Hero Association camp.","---","Inside the temporary camp.","Researchers immediately noticed the commotion.","Mike, the leader of the investigation team, looked toward the charging monsters.","His face instantly turned pale.","\"...Damn it.\"","He immediately shouted,","\"Emergency protocol! Everyone to your assigned positions! Activate the containment barrier immediately!\"","\"Move!\"","The Hero Association staff sprang into action. Long before beginning their investigation.","They had anticipated the possibility of a dungeon breach.","Specialized mana devices had been buried around the dungeon entrance in a perfect circle.","Their sole purpose was to contain exactly this kind of disaster.","At Mike’s command the devices activated simultaneously. Brilliant streams of blue mana erupted into the sky.","One by one the beams connected together.","A gigantic dome-shaped barrier rapidly formed around the entire dungeon entrance.","Just before the barrier completely sealed...","Gareth, Liana and the injured mage, Selena.","Managed to dive through the opening. The translucent blue barrier closed behind them.","The first wave of horrifying creatures slammed into it with earth-shaking force.","BOOOOOOM!!","The entire dome trembled. Then another monster crashed into it.","Hundreds of pale creatures were clawing, biting, and roaring against the magical barrier.","The Hero Association members could only stare in horror.","Because every one of them realized the same terrifying truth.","If that barrier failed.","Novaris City would become the monsters’ next hunting ground.","\"Sir Mike. I have contacted Novaris Academy. Fortunately Principle Adiran is present. He will come soon.\" Hearing one of the member’s words.","Mike sighed in relief. One of the strongest person in empire was present in city."]},{"number":243,"title":"Chapter 243: Monster Wave [2]","paragraphs":["Elyon City","Deep beneath Elyon City.","Inside a C-rank dungeon.","Arisha and her party were desperately fleeing through a long underground passage. The calm dungeon exploration they had expected had turned into a nightmare.","ROOOOOOAAARRRRRRR!!","A deafening roar echoed behind them. The sound was quickly followed by dozens more.","The monsters were coming. But an entire horde.","\"Don’t stop running!\" Brenett shouted from the front of the group.","The tall greatsword user tightened his grip around his massive blade while glancing over his shoulder.","\"They’re gaining on us!\"","The party had entered the dungeon several hours earlier.","Everything had gone according to plan at first.","They had defeated the dungeon’s native monsters one after another while steadily advancing deeper underground.","Then without warning. The ground had split open.","Cracks spread throughout the dungeon floor. From beneath the earth those creatures had emerged.","The same horrifying monsters.","Pale, oily white skin. Long arms ending in black claws. Seven black horns. They simply kept coming.","No matter how many they killed. More climbed out from underground. Realizing they would eventually be overwhelmed...","Brenett had immediately ordered a retreat.","Now the five of them were fighting while running for their lives.","Arisha suddenly glanced backward. The monsters were almost upon them.","She immediately planted one foot firmly against the ground. Her bow was already drawn.","Mana surged into the string.","She released it.","SWISH!!","A single arrow streaked through the air like a bolt of lightning. But it was covered with dense azure mana.","Mid-flight the mana surrounding it exploded.","One arrow became many. More than ten radiant mana arrows spread across the passage before descending upon the charging monsters.","Weapon Art—Sky Hunter.","Second Form: Thousand Feather Rain.","Every arrow flew with deadly precision.","SHRK!","SHRK!","SHRK!","Several monsters had their shoulders pierced. Others were struck through their thighs.","A few were hit directly in the eyes. The barrage briefly slowed the front ranks.","\"Keep moving!\"","Arisha shouted as she immediately resumed running.","Beside her...","Emma clenched both fists. Brown mana flowed around her gauntlets.","The stone beneath her feet suddenly rose. Chunks of rock wrapped around her fists, forming thick stone armor.","At the same time several pillars of earth erupted from the ground behind them.","BOOM!","The stone pillars blocked the narrow corridor. Several charging monsters slammed directly into them.","The passage collapsed partially, burying a handful of creatures beneath falling rocks.","\"It won’t hold them long!\"","Emma warned.","\"They’re breaking through already!\"","As if proving her words the creatures smashed apart the earth pillars with terrifying brute strength.","Behind them Piara raised her wand.","Blue mana circles rapidly appeared around its tip. \"Ice Spears!\"","More than a dozen icy lances shot backward. They pierced through several monsters before shattering into freezing mist.","The creatures slowed only slightly. Their numbers barely changed.","\"Damn it...\"","Piara’s breathing had become ragged. Mana exhaustion was beginning to catch up to her.","Ricky remained at the rear of the group. The dual-dagger wielder moved like a shadow. Whenever a monster got too close he instantly appeared before it.","His twin daggers flashed.","Slash!","A creature’s throat split open. He kicked its body backward into the monsters chasing behind it before immediately retreating.","\"Move! They’re surrounding us!\"","Brenett suddenly stopped. Turning around, he planted his feet firmly against the stone floor.","His enormous greatsword was raised high above his shoulder.","Mana erupted around the blade. With a furious roar.","He swung.","BOOOOOOM!!","A gigantic sword wave tore through the tunnel. The front line of monsters was sent flying.","Several crashed into the walls while others were sliced apart. Yet even that overwhelming attack failed to stop the horde.","Piara, Ricky and Brenett were condensed core rank adventurers. But they were still weak for fighting this many monsters head on.","More creatures climbed over the bodies of their fallen companions. They showed no fear.","No hesitation.","Only hunger.","Brenett clicked his tongue. \"...Damn monsters.\"","He turned immediately.","\"Run!\"","The five continued sprinting through the dungeon. None of them remained uninjured. A long claw mark stretched across Brenett’s left shoulder, staining his armor with blood.","Arisha’s right forearm bore several fresh cuts from narrowly avoiding a monster’s claws. Her righ forearm had three scratches from those creatures. Blood stream down from it.","Emma’s breathing had become heavy, and blood dripped steadily from a bite wound on her calf.","Piara’s robe was torn across her side, exposing a bleeding gash beneath.","Even Ricky, despite his speed, had several deep scratches across his back where a monster had nearly caught him.","They were exhausted. Their mana was rapidly running dry.","Yet behind them. The horrifying creatures continued pouring through the underground passage without end.","Like an endless tide of nightmares.","For the first time since becoming adventurers. Every member of the party realized the same terrifying truth.","This wasn’t a normal dungeon outbreak. Something far more terrifying had begun.","----","Ebonreach Duchy","At the heart of the Duchy of Ebonreach stood its capital...","Silverbrook City.","The home of House Nightfall.","Normally, its streets bustled with merchants, adventurers, and nobles going about their daily lives. Today it had become a battlefield.","Only a short while earlier without the slightest warning. The earth had shaken violently. Not throughout the entire city only within the bustling commercial district.","At first, the citizens believed it was nothing more than an ordinary earthquake.","Then the ground split apart.","BOOOOOOM!!","A deafening crack echoed across the district. The stone-paved streets ruptured as a gigantic fissure tore through the city.","Buildings tilted.","Roads collapsed.","Market stalls were swallowed whole.","The crack stretched for hundreds of meters, tearing through houses, warehouses, and even the underground utility tunnels beneath the city.","No one could see its bottom.","It disappeared into absolute darkness.","Then aomething climbed out. The first creature emerged from the abyss. An endless stream of pale monsters poured from the underground fissure.","They spread through the city like a flood.","\"AAAAAHHHHH!!\"","Terrified screams echoed from every direction.","The monsters didn’t hesitate. They attacked anyone they saw.","A merchant tried shielding himself with a wooden cart. One creature ripped straight through it.","Another grabbed him before sinking its grotesque teeth into his shoulder. His scream lasted only seconds. Nearby a mother desperately clutched her young daughter.","\"No! Someone help us! Please!\"","She tried to run. She never made it. One of the creatures pounced from the side.","Blood splattered across the street. \"My child!!\"","The mother’s desperate scream echoed through the district. The little girl reached toward her. Before another monster seized her as well.","Children. Elderly people. Merchants. Travelers. None were spared.","Panic spread faster than the monsters themselves. Fortunately the Knights of House Nightfall responded almost immediately.","\"Protect the civilians!\"","\"Evacuate everyone!\"","\"Move them toward the northern district!\"","Groups of black-armored knights rushed through the streets, forming defensive lines between the monsters and fleeing civilians.","City security squads joined them without hesitation.","Magic illuminated the streets. Arrows flew overhead. Swords clashed against claws.","One monster fell.","Three more emerged from the fissure. The numbers simply refused to decrease. It was an endless tide. To make matters worse the city’s strongest protector wasn’t even there.","Duke Lionel Nightfall was still away from Silverbrook.","The responsibility of defending the capital now rested entirely upon the knights. Several rooftops away a shadow rippled silently atop a small stone building overlooking the battlefield.","The darkness expanded. From within it a figure stepped out. A man dressed entirely in black.","Black coat. Black gloves. Black boots. Even a black mask concealed his face. It was Shadow. Standing beside him was Kaelan Nightfall.","The young heir stared at the burning streets below. His fists clenched so tightly that his knuckles turned white.","\"My city...\"","His voice trembled.","\"They’re killing everyone...\"","His eyes followed the countless pale creatures flooding from the enormous fissure.","There were simply too many. Even the Nightfall Knights were slowly being overwhelmed.","Shadow quietly observed the battlefield. Then he sighed.","\"Looks like I arrived a little too late.\"","He glanced sideways at Kaelan.","\"I can still save your city. I can stop this before even more innocent people die.\"","Kaelan immediately turned toward him.","\"And what do you want in return?\"","Shadow smiled beneath his mask.","\"Join me. My organization.\"","Silence.","Kaelan stared at him.","\"So... If I refuse... You won’t help them?\"","Shadow laughed.","\"Heh. You’re misunderstanding me.\" He folded his arms. \"I’ll help regardless. I have no desire to watch innocent people die.\"","His gaze returned to the battlefield.","\"But... I’d like you to witness my strength with your own eyes. Perhaps then... You’ll truly understand why joining me is the right choice.\"","Kaelan looked back toward the streets below. Another explosion echoed through the city. More screams followed. He clenched his jaw.","\"Fine.\" His voice was cold. \"If you really can save them... I’ll join your organization.\"","For the first time.","\"Good. A wise decision.\"","Then he added with a chuckle,","\"And don’t think you’re getting a free ride.\"","He looked directly at Kaelan.","\"You’re fighting too. You need to train as well and experience how to fight in such situations.\"","Before Kaelan could respond. Shadow’s own shadow spread rapidly beneath their feet. It swallowed both of them whole.","The rooftop became empty once more. As though neither of them had ever been there. Only the distant screams of Silverbrook continued echoing across the city."]},{"number":244,"title":"Chapter 244: Monster Wave [3]","paragraphs":["Kaelan dashed through the ruined streets of Silverbrook.","Mana coiled around both of his daggers like living shadows. His eyes remained fixed on the monsters pouring endlessly from the massive fissure.","\"Die!\"","He lunged toward the nearest creature.","Slash!","Both daggers carved across its chest. Dark color mana exploded upon impact. The monster staggered backward but it didn’t fall. Only several shallow cuts marked its pale, oily skin.","\"...Damn it.\"","Kaelan clicked his tongue.","\"These monsters are incredibly tough.\"","Their flesh was far harder than ordinary monsters. His darkness-enhanced attacks could injure them, but they lacked the power to cut deeply through their bodies.","The only reliable way to kill them was by targeting their vital points.","Their neck, their eyes or piercing directly into the brain.","Unfortunately none of those were easy targets against creatures that moved so violently.","Another monster charged. Kaelan lowered his body, slipped beneath its claws, and slashed upward toward its neck.","SHRK!","His blade cut halfway through.","The monster let out a distorted scream. Before it could recover, Kaelan spun behind it and drove his second dagger into the back of its neck.","CRACK!","The creature collapsed. He had barely taken a breath.","SWISH!!","\"...!\"","A burning pain erupted across his face. One of the monsters had silently circled behind him. Its black claws tore across his cheek before he could react.","Blood splashed onto the ground.","\"Argh!!\"","Kaelan staggered several steps backward, instinctively placing a hand over the fresh wound. Warm blood trickled between his fingers. His vision blurred for a split second.","A familiar amused voice echoed nearby.","\"Hey, Kaelan. You should pay attention to your surroundings while fighting. What are you doing, buddy?\"","Shadow casually walked through the battlefield with his hands tucked inside his coat pockets. His movements were completely relaxed.","Almost leisurely. It was as though he were taking an evening stroll instead of walking through a battlefield.","Even stranger the monsters hesitated.","Whenever one approached Shadow. It instinctively slowed down.","Some even stepped backward. Almost as if they feared him.","Kaelan noticed it immediately. ’Why aren’t they attacking him...?’","By now most civilians had already been evacuated by the Nightfall Knights. Only scattered battles remained throughout the district.","Kaelan and Shadow had unknowingly reached the area closest to the gigantic fissure. The monsters emerging from underground were the most numerous here.","Yet no knights had managed to arrive. Not even Captain Drake Steelborn. The endless tide of creatures continued pouring from the crack.","Kaelan looked around.","Dozens of monsters were closing in.","\"...Damn it.\"","Without another thought, he turned and sprinted toward Shadow.","\"Oi! Help me!!\"","The instant he ran past one of the towering monsters lunged from behind. Its enormous claws descended toward Kaelan’s exposed back.","It was too close.","Kaelan couldn’t dodge. Then a thin black line flashed through the air.","It was so fast. He barely saw it.","SHRRRK!!","The monster froze. A heartbeat later. Its body split cleanly down the middle. Both halves slid apart before crashing onto the street.","Dark blood flooded the broken pavement.","Kaelan stared in disbelief.","\"...What?\"","Shadow hadn’t even looked at it.","He simply sighed.","\"So impatient.\"","He lazily raised one hand. Then he flicked a single finger.","Nothing happened for one brief moment.","The battlefield became silent.","Then hundreds of razor-thin shadow slashes materialized out of thin air. They spread across the battlefield like invisible threads.","SHRRRK!!","SHRRRK!!","SHRRRK!!","The attacks swept through the streets with terrifying precision. Every monster within nearly a hundred-meter radius was struck simultaneously.","Some were bisected. Others were cut into three or four pieces. Heads rolled across the ground. Limbs flew through the air. Blood erupted everywhere.","Within a single second more than a hundred monsters had been reduced to lifeless pieces scattered across the ruined streets.","Silence followed.","Kaelan stood completely frozen. His mouth slowly fell open.","\"...How...\"","He couldn’t even comprehend what he had just witnessed.","One attack one casual flick of a finger. And an entire battlefield had been erased.","Shadow looked down at his own hand.","\"Hmm... It’s been a while.\"","He smiled faintly. \"I suppose I’ve relied on magic a little too much lately.\"","A sword slowly formed within his right hand. Not forged from steel but from pure darkness.","The blade seemed to absorb the surrounding light, its edge so black that it almost vanished against the shadows around it.","Shadow casually swung it once.","\"Let’s fight properly for a change.\"","The next instant he disappeared. Not with a flash. Not with teleportation. He simply moved so fast that it look like he vanished.","Kaelan’s eyes darted across the battlefield.","\"...Where?\"","He couldn’t find him. Not even for a fraction of a second.","SHRRRK!!","A monster several dozen meters away was suddenly cut in half.","Another lost its head. Another exploded into pieces.","Bodies continued collapsing one after another. Every few moments a black flash appeared somewhere else. Each flash was followed by another monster dying.","Shadow moved so quickly that even Kaelan’s enhanced eyesight couldn’t track him.","All Kaelan could see were monsters collapsing across the battlefield as if an invisible executioner were walking among them.","Kaelan truly understood what overwhelming strength looked like. And it terrified him.","’He really is stronger than my father.’ He thought.","---","Meanwhile.","Back to Damien.","He remained hidden behind the thick trunk of a towering tree, struggling to catch his breath. His entire body ached. His clothes were torn and stained with blood.","The wounds from the battle against the giant guardian still hadn’t fully healed. Beyond the forest the horde of pale monsters continued charging toward Everhold City.","Their deafening roars echoed through the woods as they crushed everything in their path.","\"...Damn...\"","Damien gripped his sword tightly. He wanted to fight. But in his current condition.","He could barely stand.","Then a gigantic magic circle suddenly appeared high above the battlefield. Its intricate runes glowed with deep violet light. The monsters below instinctively looked upward.","The next moment. Darkness gathered beneath the magic circle.","It condensed rapidly. A massive sphere of compressed darkness formed in midair. It continued growing larger until it resembled a small meteor.","It fell.","BOOOOOOOOM!!","The sphere slammed into the charging horde. A violent explosion of darkness erupted in every direction. The earth shook. Trees were uprooted.","Dozens of monsters were swallowed by the blast before being torn apart by countless shadow blades hidden within the explosion.","Black blood sprayed across the forest.","Damien’s tired eyes brightened.","\"Master...She came.\""]},{"number":245,"title":"Chapter 245: Monster Wave [4]","paragraphs":["He immediately stepped out from behind the tree, searching the surrounding forest.","A moment later he found her.","Morgana stood silently upon the branch of a towering tree overlooking the battlefield.","Her purple eyes calmly scanned the horde below. Searching. Looking for one particular person. Then her gaze met Damien’s.","Without the slightest hesitation she stepped forward. Rather than falling she kicked off the branch. Her body became a blur. While descending, she reached into her storage ring.","A long dark-purple spear appeared in her hand. Before touching the ground. She swung it once.","A crescent of dark mana swept across the battlefield.","SHRRRK!!","Several monsters were sliced cleanly in half before they even realized she had arrived.","She landed gracefully. Without slowing down. She continued running. Every monster that approached her died in a single strike. Within seconds she stood before Damien.","Her sharp eyes quickly examined his injuries.","\"...Damien. Are you alright?\"","Damien nodded weakly.","\"...Yes...I’m fine...But...\"","Before he could continue. Morgana interrupted him. Her voice remained calm. \"...Where is Noah?\"","The question made Damien’s expression fall.","He lowered his head.","\"...I...I don’t know.\"","His fists slowly clenched. \"After we defeated the guardian...A portal suddenly appeared on the final floor. It pulled Noah inside. I tried to reach him... But before I could... The portal disappeared.\"","Silence.","Morgana’s grip around her spear tightened.","Her jaw clenched. \"...Damn it.\"","She looked toward the monsters still pouring from the forest.","\"I already informed Duke Lionel after detecting these creatures leaving the labyrinth. He should have begun preparing Everhold City’s defenses by now.\"","She turned back toward Damien.","\"Until reinforcements arrive... I need every detail. Tell me everything that happened inside the labyrinth. Don’t leave anything out.\"","Damien nodded.","Then he began recounting everything. From the very first floor... To Noah’s disappearance.","---","Everhold City","At the massive defensive wall surrounding Everhold...","Knights hurried across the battlements.","Orders echoed continuously.","\"Activate the eastern barrier!\"","\"Archers to your positions!\"","\"Mages, prepare long-range spells!\"","The city’s ancient defensive mechanism had already been activated. Towering pillars surrounding Everhold released brilliant streams of mana into the sky.","The beams connected together. A colossal translucent barrier gradually enveloped the entire city. It shimmered faintly beneath the afternoon sun.","Standing atop the wall was Duke Lionel Thornveil.His emerald eyes remained fixed upon the distant forest. His sword rested quietly at his waist.","His expression was unusually serious. The approaching horde was still several kilometers away.","Even from this distance. He could see countless pale figures racing through the trees.","One of the knights approached him before respectfully kneeling.","\"My Lord... Lady Morgana is still outside the barrier.\"","Lionel remained calm.","\"It’s fine. She’s more than capable of protecting herself. Those monsters won’t pose much of a threat to her.\"","His gaze remained fixed upon the advancing horde.","Then his eyes narrowed.","\"...They look identical.\"","The knight looked confused.","\"Identical, my Lord?\"","Lionel nodded slowly.","\"The photographs. The ones I received from the Hero Association. The sleeping creatures discovered beneath the dungeon in Novaris City...\"","He slowly drew a breath.","\"...These are the same monsters.\"","---","Back to Damien and Morgana.","\"...What did you just say?\"","Shock appeared on Morgana’s face.","She stared directly at Damien. Her purple eyes widened.","\"Everything you’ve just described...The labyrinth...The floors...The monsters...\"","She slowly shook her head.","\"...None of them were there.\"","Damien froze.","\"...What?\"","Morgana continued,","\"I explored that labyrinth before you two entered. I explored all floors.\"","Her voice grew increasingly solemn.","\"But the labyrinth you described...Is completely different. The forest. The submerged city. The undead fortress. The library of riddles. The giant guardian. I’ve never seen any of them. They simply...didn’t exist.\"","Damien’s pupils contracted.","His breathing stopped for a moment.","\"That’s impossible.\"","He stared blankly at Morgana. If she was telling the truth...","Then the labyrinth Noah and he had explored was no longer the same labyrinth she had entered years ago.","Somehow it had changed after Noah and Damien entered it.","---","Holy Duchy","The disaster was no longer confined to a single place.","Across the Empire similar outbreaks had begun appearing one after another.","Monstrous hordes erupted from beneath cities, villages, and ancient dungeons, spreading chaos wherever they emerged.","Not even the Holy Duchy was spared.","Fortunately the duchy’s capital, Caeloria City, remained untouched.","Its divine barriers and vigilant defenders kept the city safe. And there was no outbreak of those monsters near the city.","However, many smaller cities and villages throughout the Holy Duchy weren’t as fortunate.","One of the hardest-hit locations was Krios, the nearest city to the capital.","The peaceful city had descended into complete chaos.","Pale monsters rampaged through the streets, tearing through buildings and chasing terrified civilians.","Screams echoed from every direction. Yet, unlike many other cities across the Empire.","Krios was not without hope.","The Church had responded almost immediately.","Groups of Holy Paladins clad in gleaming silver armour formed defensive lines throughout the city, shielding civilians while battling the endless tide of monsters.","Golden divine magic illuminated the streets as priests continuously healed the wounded behind the front lines.","Leading the Church’s forces was the Pope himself.","Lucian.","Upon receiving reports of the outbreak, Lucian had personally travelled to Krios alongside his daughters and a handful of his most trusted subordinates.","Thanks to their swift arrival, the situation had gradually come under control.","The monsters were still numerous...","But the city was no longer on the verge of collapse.","Standing amidst the battlefield, Lucian calmly surveyed the surroundings.","His white robes fluttered gently in the wind as explosions and battle cries echoed in the distance.","After a brief moment, he turned toward his eldest daughter.","\"Lyria.\"","She immediately stepped forward.","\"Yes, Father?\"","Lucian’s expression remained calm and composed.","\"The battle here is stabilising. It’s time for you to fulfil your role.\"","He looked toward the countless injured civilians and exhausted paladins being carried away from the battlefield.","\"Gather every healer we brought. Lead the medical teams. Treat every wounded civilian and every injured knight. Make sure they’re evacuated to a safe location. You’ll be in command of the healing operation here.\"","Lyria placed a hand over her chest and bowed respectfully.","\"Yes, Father. I won’t disappoint you.\"","Her beautiful blue eyes shone with determination.","Without another word, she immediately began issuing orders.","\"Healers, with me! Split into teams of five! Priests, establish treatment stations in the northern district. The seriously injured come first!\"","The Church’s healers quickly followed her commands, rushing toward the wounded scattered throughout the city.","Watching his daughter leave, Lucian gave a slight nod before turning back toward the battlefield.","His gaze settled upon the largest concentration of monsters.","Hundreds of grotesque creatures were still clashing with the Holy Paladins.","Lucian slowly raised one hand toward the sky.","Immediately an enormous golden magic circle materialised high above the battlefield.","Its intricate divine runes spread across the heavens, covering hundreds of metres.","A holy pressure descended upon the entire city.","Every monster instinctively looked upward. Within the glowing magic circle...","Countless swords of pure white light began to form.","One after another. Then another. Until hundreds of radiant blades floated silently above the battlefield.","Each sword radiated overwhelming divine energy. The monsters let out furious roars.","Lucian calmly lowered his hand.","[Judgment]","At his command the countless holy swords descended.","WHOOSH!","They rained from the heavens like divine punishment.","BOOM!","SHRRRK!","BOOM!","One sword pierced through a monster’s skull.","Another split a creature cleanly in half.","Several more impaled groups of monsters simultaneously before erupting into bursts of holy light.","The battlefield shook violently beneath the relentless barrage.","Within moments hundreds of monsters had been annihilated.","The Holy Paladins could only stare in awe.","Even after witnessing the Pope’s strength countless times.","The sight of such overwhelming divine power never failed to leave them speechless."]},{"number":246,"title":"Chapter 246: Somewhere Unknown","paragraphs":["A gentle breeze drifted across a crystal-clear lake, creating delicate ripples that shimmered beneath the sunlight.","The water was so transparent that the smooth stones resting at the bottom were clearly visible.","Its gentle current produced a peaceful melody as it flowed through the surrounding wilderness.","Encircling the lake stood a dense forest of towering emerald trees, their branches swaying softly in the wind. Vibrant wildflowers bloomed across the lush grass, filling the air with a faint, pleasant fragrance.","Above...","The sky stretched endlessly, a brilliant shade of blue without a single cloud to interrupt its serenity.","It was a place untouched by war.","Untouched by monsters.","Untouched by chaos.","Lying unconscious upon the soft grass beside the lake was a young man with snow-white hair.","Noah.","His fingers twitched slightly. A moment later his eyelids slowly opened.","Brilliant blue eyes reflected the clear sky overhead. For several seconds, he simply lay there, silently staring upward.","\"...\"","Then","\"Argh...!\"","A sharp wave of pain surged through his entire body. Every muscle protested. His ribs ached. His shoulders burned. His head throbbed.","Even breathing sent dull pain through his chest. He instinctively clenched his teeth as memories flooded back into his mind.","The battle. The giant guardian. The mysterious portal. How he was sucked into that portal.","\"...Damn it...\"","His voice was hoarse.","\"Where am I?\"","He slowly looked around, confusion filling his expression. \"The portal... Where did it bring me?\"","With considerable effort, Noah planted one hand against the ground and pushed himself into a sitting position.","The movement alone caused another jolt of pain to shoot through his body. \"...Tch.\"","He examined himself. Most of his wounds had begun closing naturally. The cuts were no longer bleeding heavily.","The bruises had faded slightly. It wasn’t complete healing. But it was enough that he could still move.","He gently pressed against his ribs. A sharp pain immediately answered him. \"...Did I break something?\"","He frowned.","\"I can’t tell.\"","Without proper medical equipment—or healing magic—there was no way to know for certain. After resting for another minute, Noah slowly stood up.","His legs wobbled slightly before regaining their balance. His throat suddenly felt unbearably dry. Only then did he notice the crystal-clear lake a short distance away.","He slowly walked toward it, careful not to aggravate his injuries.","Kneeling at the water’s edge. He leaned forward and cupped both hands together. Cool water filled his palms. He brought it to his lips.","The refreshing water slid gently down his throat, washing away the dryness that had lingered since the battle.","\"...Ah...\"","He let out a quiet sigh of relief. It tasted remarkably pure. Unlike ordinary river water, it carried an almost refreshing sweetness.","He scooped up another handful before splashing it across his face. The cool sensation instantly washed away the remaining dizziness.","His mind became noticeably clearer. For a while he simply sat beside the peaceful lake. Listening to the gentle sound of flowing water.","Trying to organize his thoughts. \"...Am I still inside the labyrinth? Did I enter some new floor?\"","He looked toward the surrounding forest. \"...Or did that portal send me somewhere else entirely?\"","There was only one way to find out. Waiting here wouldn’t give him any answers.","Noah slowly rose to his feet once more. \"...Let’s have a look around.\"","Taking careful, measured steps, he entered the forest. His body remained weak, forcing him to walk much slower than usual.","Even so the scenery around him gradually eased his tense mind.","\"...This place is beautiful.\"","Sunlight filtered through the dense canopy above, painting shifting patterns across the forest floor. The air felt incredibly fresh.","Birds chirped peacefully among the branches. Leaves rustled gently with every passing breeze.","There was no smell of blood. No distant roars. No signs of destruction.","It felt alive.","As Noah continued walking, something caught his attention. A white rabbit suddenly darted across the path before disappearing into a patch of bushes.","He blinked. \"A rabbit?\"","Moments later... A small family of deer cautiously emerged from between the trees. They quietly drank from a nearby stream before disappearing deeper into the forest.","Noah stood frozen for a moment. \"...Actual animals...\"","His surprise was genuine.","Ever since entering the labyrinth, every living creature he had encountered had been some form of magical beast or monster.","But these these were ordinary wildlife.","They carried no trace of mana. No hostility. Just peaceful animals living their lives.","A faint smile appeared on Noah’s face. \"At least food won’t be a problem.\"","His gaze wandered deeper into the seemingly endless forest.","\"...But where exactly am I?\"","The question remained unanswered.","For now there was little he could do except continue exploring. Perhaps somewhere within this mysterious land. He would eventually discover the truth behind where the portal had brought him.","Noah continued deeper into the mysterious forest.","The gentle breeze rustled the emerald leaves overhead, while rays of sunlight filtered through the dense canopy, painting shifting patterns across the ground.","His footsteps remained slow. Every movement still caused a dull ache to spread through his battered body.","\"...I really overdid it.\"","He pressed a hand against his ribs before letting out a small sigh. Although the pain hadn’t disappeared, it had become manageable.","His mana had also recovered considerably while resting beside the lake. Not enough for a prolonged battle. But enough to defend himself if necessary.","After walking for nearly half an hour, his stomach growled loudly.","\"...Right. I haven’t eaten since before entering the labyrinth.\"","Only then did he realize just how hungry he was. Fortunately, nature seemed surprisingly generous. Ahead stood a tall tree covered in clusters of bright crimson fruit.","The fruits resembled oversized apples, their skins smooth and glistening beneath the sunlight.","Noah stopped beneath the tree and observed them carefully.","\"No signs of poison...\"","At least none that he could recognize. Plucking one from a low branch, he inspected it for a few moments before taking a cautious bite.","Crunch.","Sweet juice filled his mouth instantly.","His eyes widened.","\"...Not bad.\"","In fact it was delicious. The fruit carried a refreshing sweetness with a faint citrus-like aftertaste. After eating several of them, the emptiness in his stomach finally eased.","He gathered a few more into his storage ring before continuing onward.","Hours passed.","Whenever the pain in his body became too much, Noah would stop beneath a tree, rest for several minutes, and then continue walking.","As time went on the tension in his shoulders gradually faded.","At first, he’d expected monsters to leap from every shadow.","But nothing happened. Instead he encountered only peaceful wildlife.","Rabbits darted between bushes. Colorful birds flew overhead.","Small foxes watched him curiously before disappearing into the undergrowth.","It was almost difficult to believe this place had anything to do with the terrifying labyrinth.","\"...Maybe this really isn’t a dungeon.\"","The thought crossed his mind more than once.","Eventually the forest opened.","A wide river stretched before him, its crystal-clear water flowing steadily from north to south. The opposite bank was visible, though noticeably darker. The trees there were much taller.","Much older.","Their dense canopies blocked out most of the sunlight.","\"Hm...\"","Noah had no desire to swim with his injuries. Instead, pale-blue mana gathered beneath his feet.","A thin sheet of ice spread across the river’s surface. The frozen path extended steadily toward the opposite shore.","Satisfied, Noah stepped onto it.","Each footstep caused another layer of ice to form ahead of him, creating a stable bridge across the flowing water.","Within moments, he reached the other side. The instant he entered the darker forest...","Something felt different.","He frowned.","\"...It’s quiet.\"","Too quiet.","The cheerful chirping of birds had vanished. There were no animals here. It was silent.","His hand slowly rested on the hilt of his sword. The vegetation here was unlike anything he had seen before.","Leaves were broader. Flowers were enormous. Some stood taller than a person. Others resembled strange blossoms with thick, fleshy petals.","One flower directly ahead reached nearly twice Noah’s height. Its crimson petals were folded neatly together around a bulb-like center.","\"...What kind of plant is that?\"","Curiosity overcame caution for a brief moment.","He stepped closer. Its surface appeared strangely smooth..","Noah slowly turned his head.Only then did he notice that similar giant plants were scattered throughout the forest.","Some resembled flowers. Others looked more like enormous vines rooted deep into the earth.","\"This place...\"","His instincts suddenly screamed.","Without thinking he threw himself sideways.","BOOM!","The giant flower exploded open where he had been standing moments earlier. Its petals unfolded into a grotesque, circular maw lined with rows of thorn-like spikes. The enormous bloom slammed shut with tremendous force, narrowly missing him.","\"What the—?!\"","Noah rolled across the ground before pushing himself back to his feet. The giant flower swayed violently. Though rooted firmly to the earth, it twisted its stem as if searching for another chance to strike.","\"So it can’t move...\"","He had barely finished the thought.","Rustle.","Movement erupted from his left. Another massive plant unfurled.","Then another. Thick green vines shot through the air like whips.","\"Damn it!\"","Noah reached into his storage ring. His sword appeared instantly in his hand. Blue mana flowed along the blade, sharpening its edge with a thin layer of ice.","The first vine reached him.","Slash!","The blade cut cleanly through it. A second attacked from behind. He pivoted despite the pain in his ribs and severed it with another swing.","More vines burst from every direction. There were too many.","Noah abandoned the idea of fighting.","Instead, he sprinted through the forest, weaving between towering trees while cutting away every vine that threatened to entangle him.","His battered body protested with every step. Pain shot through his chest. His breathing became heavier.","Yet he couldn’t afford to slow down. Behind him the strange forest had awakened. And it clearly had no intention of letting him leave."]},{"number":247,"title":"Chapter 247: What in the World...?","paragraphs":["Noah burst out of the dense forest, his breathing ragged.","The oppressive silence behind him gradually faded as he crossed back into the peaceful woodland he had explored earlier.","A few more hurried steps later. The crystal-clear river came into view once again.","He slowed to a stop and looked toward the frozen path stretching across its surface. Something like a bridge of ice remained intact.","Despite the river’s steady current, the mana-infused ice had yet to melt away.","Noah let out a quiet sigh of relief.","\"What luck I have.\"","His voice carried equal parts amusement and exhaustion.","After everything he had experienced since arriving in this mysterious place. Simply finding a safe route back felt like a blessing.","He glanced once toward the dark forest across the river. The towering trees stood silently beneath the dim sky.","Nothing moved. Nothing made a sound.","Yet Noah had no intention of returning there. \"There’s no reason to throw myself into danger.\"","He stepped onto the frozen bridge. The ice remained firm beneath his feet as he calmly crossed back to the opposite bank.","The moment he entered the familiar forest, the atmosphere changed completely. A cool breeze rustled the leaves overhead.","Birds chirped somewhere among the branches. Small animals cautiously peeked out from the bushes before disappearing once they noticed him.","Compared to the sinister forest across the river. This place felt almost comforting.","\"I’ll find somewhere to rest for tonight.\"","Although one thing continued bothering him.","Noah looked up toward the sky. It remained brilliantly bright.","Yet there was no sun. Not even a faint outline of one. The light seemed to come from everywhere at once, bathing the entire forest in a soft, constant glow.","\"Strange. I’ve been walking for hours. But the sky has changed.. but can’t see where sun is..\"","His brows furrowed. \"Maybe I’m still inside the labyrinth after all.\"","It was the only explanation that made any sense. Labyrinths often ignored the natural laws of the outside world.","Artificial skies. Distorted landscapes. Even warped time.","None of those were unheard of. Still this place felt far too alive to resemble any dungeon Noah had ever heard of. Unable to reach a conclusion, he continued walking.","Eventually the familiar lake came into view. Its crystal-clear waters remained as peaceful as before, reflecting the endless blue sky above.","This was where he had awakened after passing through the mysterious portal.","For now it was the safest place he knew.","Noah walked toward a large tree near the water’s edge and slowly lowered himself against its sturdy trunk.","The rough bark pressed comfortably against his back. He simply stared across the tranquil lake.","\"...How am I supposed to contact Damien?\"","He sighed softly. \"Did he end up here too or am I the only one who was pulled through that portal?\"","The uncertainty weighed heavily on his mind.","If Damien had remained outside. He was probably searching for him. If this truly was another section of the labyrinth. Then there had to be an exit somewhere.","\"I should look for it.\"","His gaze lowered to the bandages wrapped around his body.","\"But not like this.\"","Every movement still sent pain through his battered muscles. His injuries had improved slightly, but they were far from healed.","Searching an unknown area in this condition would only increase his chances of getting killed. \"...First things first.\"","He reached toward his storage ring. After searching through its contents, he found exactly what he had hoped was still there.","A single vial. A low-grade healing potion.","He had deliberately saved it during the labyrinth expedition in case of an emergency. \"...Looks like this is that emergency.\"","Without hesitation, he uncorked the bottle. The crimson liquid shimmered faintly.","Noah drank it in one gulp. Warmth immediately spread through his body. The dull ache in his muscles gradually eased.","The cuts across his arms stopped throbbing. Even the pain around his ribs became noticeably lighter.","It wasn’t enough to restore him completely. But it was far better than before.","\"That’s all I’ve got.\"","He glanced toward the lake one last time. \"I’ll recover as much as I can before moving again.\"","Noah adjusted his position beneath the tree, allowing himself to relax for the first time since arriving in this strange land.","The gentle breeze drifted across the water. The soothing sound of flowing waves echoed softly in the distance.","For the first time in days. There were no battles. There were no monsters. No desperate struggle for survival.","There was only peace. His eyelids gradually grew heavier. \"...Just a short rest...\"","He murmured quietly, within minutes exhaustion finally claimed him.","Leaning against the ancient tree. Noah drifted into a deep, dreamless sleep as the tranquil forest continued its silent vigil around the crystal-clear lake.","---","THUNDER!!","A deafening clap of thunder echoed across the sky.","THUNDER!!","Noah’s eyelids twitched. A cold breeze brushed against his face.","Because of his Ice Affinity, he couldn’t truly feel the cold. His body naturally resisted low temperatures.","Even so he could sense the sudden change in the atmosphere.","The air had become heavier. It was sharper.","His eyes snapped open. \"...\"","The peaceful blue sky that had greeted him before was gone. It wasn’t night. Instead, an endless blanket of dark gray clouds had swallowed the heavens.","Blue streaks of lightning crawled across the clouds like giant serpents, briefly illuminating the world below.","Their brilliant flashes reflected in Noah’s sapphire-blue eyes.","A heartbeat later.","BOOOOOOOM!!","Thunder rolled across the entire forest.","Noah immediately pushed himself to his feet. A powerful gust of wind swept through the trees.","WHOOSH!","Towering branches bent violently. Countless leaves rustled together, creating a loud, almost eerie chorus that echoed throughout the forest.","The wind struck Noah head-on. He instinctively raised an arm to shield his face as his white hair whipped wildly behind him.","\"...Looks like a heavy storm is coming.\"","His eyes scanned the surrounding area. There wasn’t a single cave.","No rocky overhang. Nothing that could serve as shelter.","\"...Should I make one?\"","The thought surfaced almost immediately.","\"An ice house.\"","He had never attempted anything like that before.","Still in theory, it was possible. His mana had recovered to nearly half its capacity after resting. Constructing a temporary shelter shouldn’t be impossible.","\"...First, I need somewhere with enough open space.\"","Without wasting another second, Noah turned and began moving through the forest. His pace gradually increased.","Stomp.","Stomp.","Stomp.","The farther he ran the stronger the wind became. The once peaceful trees now swayed violently as if struggling to remain rooted.","He couldn’t see any animal now. ’It seems they already fled to their shelters.’","Branches creaked. Leaves flew through the air.","\"...Damn it.\"","Noah pushed forward despite the growing resistance. After several minutes the forest suddenly opened.","A familiar sight appeared before him. The river unlike the narrow section he had crossed earlier, this part of the riverbank was much wider.","\"Perfect. There should be enough room here.\"","KRAAAAKK!!","Another bolt of lightning tore across the heavens. For an instant the entire world turned white.","Noah instinctively looked up. \"What in the world...?\""]},{"number":248,"title":"Chapter 248: Shelter?","paragraphs":["Far beyond the opposite side of the river. Something enormous dominated the horizon.","The clouds there had gathered into a colossal vortex. A gigantic whirlwind stretched from the earth itself all the way into the heavens, connecting the ground to the swirling storm clouds above.","Lightning continuously danced throughout the massive column. It looked less like a natural storm... And more like a catastrophe given form.","\"That’s...Impossible.\"","Noah stared in disbelief.","The sheer scale of it dwarfed everything around it. It wasn’t stationary either. The entire storm slowly advanced.","Toward him.","\"Damn...It’s coming this way.\"","Lightning flashed endlessly inside the colossal vortex, illuminating it over and over again.","Drip.","Something cold landed against Noah’s cheek. He reached up instinctively.","Rain.","Drip.","Another drop followed. Then another. Within seconds a gentle shower spread across the forest. The rain intensified rapidly.","What began as scattered droplets transformed into a relentless downpour. Rain hammered the ground so heavily that visibility shrank dramatically.","It resembled a cloudburst.","\"No time.\"","Blue mana surged from Noah’s hands. Four thick pillars of ice erupted from the earth around him.","Immediately afterward a broad slab of ice formed above them like a roof. The makeshift shelter protected him from the worst of the rain.","Water crashed against the frozen surface overhead.","Yet Noah barely noticed. His eyes remained fixed upon the approaching storm. The rain had grown so heavy that the colossal vortex was becoming difficult to see. Only the constant flashes of lightning revealed its terrifying outline.","Then his heartbeat changed.","Thump.","Thump.","Thump.","It became faster. Much faster. An overwhelming sense of dread suddenly gripped him. The feeling crawled across his skin like thousands of tiny insects.","Every instinct within his body screamed.","Danger.","Noah unconsciously took a step backward.","\"...I need to leave. I need to get as far away from that thing as possible.\"","At that exact moment another bolt of lightning split the heavens.","For a single fraction of a second. The storm was illuminated.","Noah froze.","There within the heart of the gigantic vortex...","He saw it. A silhouette. Something unimaginably massive. Its true form remained hidden behind the swirling clouds.","Only its outline could be seen. Then another flash erupted. Blue lightning briefly traced the shape of two enormous eyes.","They glowed within the storm itself watching him. Every hair on Noah’s body stood on end.","His blood seemed to freeze.","\"Fuck!\"","That single word escaped his lips almost instinctively. The next instant he moved. Without another glance behind him, Noah spun around and exploded into a sprint.","Mana surged through his legs, reinforcing every muscle. His speed increased dramatically despite the injuries that still lingered throughout his body.","He didn’t care where he was running. He ran to left then right. Didn’t care about the pain all over his muscles.","Deeper into the forest. It didn’t matter. The only thing that mattered was getting as far away from that storm as possible.","Rain lashed against his face. Branches whipped across his body. Mud splashed beneath his feet. His clothes were all drenched.","Still he never slowed behind him. Thunder roared again. His heartbeat pounded in his ears like a speeding bullet train.","For the first time since arriving in this mysterious land.","Noah wasn’t running from monsters.","He was running from something far, far worse. Something his instincts refused to even comprehend.","----","Noah didn’t dare look back.","He simply ran.","Branches whipped against his arms and shoulders as he forced his exhausted body through the storm-ravaged forest.","His breathing became increasingly ragged. Every injured muscle screamed in protest. Yet he ignored the pain. The image of those enormous lightning-formed eyes remained burned into his mind.","’Run. Keep running.’","That single thought echoed endlessly inside his head.","Minutes passed.","Noah had completely lost track of time. The storm continued roaring behind him, thunder shaking the very earth beneath his feet.","\"Haa...\"","\"Haa...\"","His vision gradually blurred. The healing potion had restored only a fraction of his strength.","After everything he had endured inside the labyrinth, his body was already at its limit. His foot caught on a thick tree root hidden beneath the rain-soaked grass.","\"...!\"","His balance vanished.","Thud!","Noah crashed hard onto the muddy ground. The impact knocked the breath from his lungs. Cold mud splashed across his face, his hands, and the front of his clothes.","He simply lay there, breathing heavily.","\"Damnation!\"","His entire body ached. Rain continued pelting his back without mercy. He clenched his teeth and slowly pushed himself upright. One trembling hand pressed against the ground while the other wiped the mud from his eyes.","\"...Get up... I can’t stop here...\"","Using a nearby tree for support, Noah forced himself back onto his feet. He took a deep breath before finally looking ahead.","His expression froze.","\"...Huh?\"","The dense forest abruptly ended. Beyond the trees lay a wide clearing.","Nestled quietly in the middle of it. Stood a single wooden house. It was neither grand nor luxurious. A simple, one-story home.","Its architecture resembled that of a traditional Japanese countryside residence. Dark wooden pillars supported a gently sloping tiled roof.","Wide wooden verandas surrounded the house. Sliding doors in the front wall, while a small stone pathway led toward the entrance. There were no papers used on house door.","Despite the violent storm surrounding the forest. The clearing itself felt strangely peaceful. The rain seemed lighter here. The wind no longer howled with the same ferocity. It was almost as though the storm deliberately avoided this place.","Noah remained motionless. His blue eyes carefully studied the house. \"Someone lives here?\"","The thought sounded absurd. Everything he had experienced since entering the mysterious portal suggested this place was isolated.","Yet the house showed signs of being maintained. The wooden walls were clean. The roof appeared undamaged. No weeds overgrew the stone path. Nothing about it looked abandoned.","His instincts immediately became conflicted. One part of him warned him not to approach.","The other reminded him that he was injured, exhausted, and standing in the middle of an unknown land with a supernatural storm closing in behind him.","\"I don’t really have many choices.\"","He glanced over his shoulder. Another distant clap of thunder rolled through the forest. The storm was still advancing.","Noah let out a slow breath.","Then, with cautious steps and one hand pulled out sword from storage ring.","He began walking toward the mysterious wooden house, every sense sharpened for whatever—or whoever— might be waiting inside."]},{"number":249,"title":"Chapter 249: Someone... Please come and find me.","paragraphs":["Noah cautiously approached the wooden house. For a brief moment, he simply stood before the entrance, listening. Only the gentle patter of rain echoed around him.","There was no footsteps or voices from inside. That means no sign that anyone was inside.","\"...Hello?\"","He called out once. His voice disappeared into the quiet house. No reply came. After waiting several more seconds, Noah slowly reached for the wooden sliding door.","He gently pushed it aside.","Creak","The old door slid open with a soft groan. Inside was a narrow wooden corridor stretching deeper into the house. The polished floorboards reflected the faint daylight filtering through an open room farther inside.","Everything was remarkably clean. There wasn’t a speck of dust anywhere.","\"Someone must still be living here.\"","Noah quietly stepped inside before sliding the entrance door shut behind him. As he looked down, he noticed his boots. They were completely covered in wet mud from running through the forest.","’I’d better not dirty the house.’","He crouched down and removed both boots, leaving them neatly beside the entrance before stepping onto the cool wooden floor in his socks.","The floor creaked softly beneath his weight.","He slowly made his way toward the open room. Every movement remained cautious. His hand rested lightly on the hilt of his sword, ready to react if necessary.","The room itself was simple. Everything had been crafted from wood.","There were wooden walls, wooden pillars and wooden furniture. There were no books. No paintings or any kind of decorations. Only the necessary things that a person needs.","It felt natural as though the house had been built using nothing except the resources available within the surrounding forest.","At the far end of the room, another sliding door stood open.","Curious, Noah walked toward it. The door led onto a small wooden veranda overlooking an inner garden.","Beyond it the forest stretched peacefully into the distance. The rain had reached this place as well.","But unlike the violent storm outside...","Here it fell gently. Soft droplets landed upon the carefully tended grass and smooth stones scattered throughout the small garden.","There were no fierce winds. No deafening thunder. Nor any towering vortex that he had seen.","Only quiet rainfall. \"Beautiful.\"","Noah leaned lightly against one of the wooden pillars.","Just moments ago the storm had looked like the end of the world. He was so afraid that he felt like dying from heart attack.","Yet from here it seemed strangely peaceful.","Almost calming.","His gaze drifted toward the distant horizon. The colossal storm still churned beyond the forest. Lightning continued flashing inside the enormous vortex.","Yet it never came any closer.","It was as though an invisible boundary surrounded the house, preventing the storm from crossing it.","\"This place is really safe...\"","His expression slowly grew thoughtful.","\"But who owns it?\"","Whoever lived here was clearly no ordinary person. \"I should look around before they return.\"","Turning away from the veranda, Noah began carefully inspecting the rest of the house. There were only a handful of rooms.","A modest kitchen. A sleeping room furnished with simple bedding. A storage room.","And finally a bathroom.","\"Nice.\"","His eyes immediately landed on a large wooden tub filled with clean water. Beside it stood several neatly arranged buckets.","Someone had prepared everything carefully. Noah looked down at himself.","His clothes were soaked. Mud covered nearly every inch of them. His armor wasn’t in much better condition. \"Might as well clean up.\"","He removed his light armor piece by piece, placing each item carefully on the floor before storing them inside his storage ring.","Then came his outer clothes. Without them, the numerous injuries covering his body became fully visible.","Long claw marks crossed his shoulders. Dark bruises spread across his ribs. Smaller cuts covered his arms and legs.","His well-defined physique bore the unmistakable signs of the battles he had survived. Taking one of the wooden buckets, Noah slowly poured cool water over himself.","The refreshing sensation washed away the dried blood, dirt, and mud clinging to his skin. He couldn’t help letting out a quiet sigh.","\"That feels much better.\"","One bucket became another.","Eventually he decided there was little point stopping halfway.","Using the stored water, Noah thoroughly cleaned himself before carefully washing the mud from his clothes and light armor as well.","Once everything was clean, he spread the damp garments neatly where they could dry later and returned his armor to his storage ring.","After drying himself with a clean cloth he found inside the bathroom, Noah changed into a spare pair of undergarments and loose trousers from his storage ring.","\"Much better.\"","Finally he felt almost comfortable. Leaving his freshly washed clothes behind to dry, Noah returned to the same room overlooking the garden.","He quietly lowered himself onto the wooden floor near the open veranda. The gentle rain continued falling outside.","Cool air drifted into the room. For several minutes he simply watched the peaceful scenery.","\"I wonder how long this storm will last.\"","His quiet voice was almost drowned out by the rainfall.","\"And...\"","He glanced around the silent house.","\"I still have no idea who lives here.\"","A faint frown appeared on his face. \"What if the owner isn’t exactly welcoming?\"","The thought made him instinctively glance toward the entrance.","Although something about the house didn’t feel hostile. It felt peaceful and safe. It was almost comforting to him.","Noah rested his chin against one hand and let out a quiet sigh. \"I’m talking to myself an awful lot lately.\"","A small, tired smile appeared on his face. \"I guess being stranded alone does that to a person.\" The only reply was the gentle rhythm of rain falling beyond the veranda.","---","Night had quietly fallen.","The violent storm that had shaken the forest for hours had finally disappeared.","For nearly an hour now only the gentle chirping of insects and the occasional rustle of leaves disturbed the silence.","Inside the mysterious wooden house. Noah had made himself as comfortable as circumstances allowed.","After the rain ended, he had searched the house more thoroughly. The kitchen, though simple, was surprisingly well stocked.","A woven basket sat neatly upon the wooden counter, filled with fresh fruit that looked as though it had been picked only recently.","\"Still fresh?\"","He picked up one of the crimson fruits and examined it. There wasn’t a single bruise on its surface.","\"Whoever lives here can’t be far away...\"","Although the thought made him hesitate for a moment, hunger eventually won.","\"I’ll apologize later.\"","He quietly ate several of the fruits. The sweet taste eased the lingering emptiness in his stomach. After cleaning up, Noah returned to the same room overlooking the garden.","The sliding door remained partially open, allowing the cool night breeze to drift inside. Moonlight illuminated the quiet courtyard.","Noah lay flat on the smooth wooden floor, using one arm as a pillow while staring absentmindedly at the wooden ceiling. Silence filled the room.","\"Hello, System.\"","There was no response.","\"System?\"","Nothing came from his calling.","He let out a tired sigh. \"Figures.\"","The mysterious system had never appeared whenever he wanted it to. It only surfaced after important events connected to the game’s storyline occurred.","Calling it was completely pointless. \"Where exactly am I?\"","He rubbed his forehead.","\"Someone... Please come find me.\"","Rolling lazily onto his side, he let out another long sigh.","\"I wonder what everyone’s doing right now.\"","His thoughts drifted toward Damien and others.","\"Hopefully Damien is safe as well.\"","That was the last thought on his mind as he quietly stared into the darkness beyond the open veranda.","While outside the house. The sky once again started to roar in thunder and storm."]},{"number":250,"title":"Chapter 250: Who Is The Owner?","paragraphs":["Outside the Labyrinth. The forest remained eerily quiet. Evening had settled over the battlefield.","Although countless monster corpses littered the ground, pale creatures continued emerging from the floating portal suspended high above the ruined clearing.","Standing atop the branch of a towering tree. Damien looked toward Morgana. His expression was filled with concern.","\"Master. What should we do now? We have no idea where Noah is.\"","Morgana remained silent for several seconds. Her amethyst eyes never left the portal.","Finally she spoke. \"I’m going in.\"","Damien immediately turned toward her. \"Master?\"","\"If that portal is still connected to the place you escaped from...There may still be clues inside.\" She tightened her grip around her dark-purple spear. \"If Noah was taken somewhere. Perhaps I’ll find traces leading to him.\"","Damien slowly nodded. \"Understood.\"","Morgana looked at him once more. \"You stay here.\"","The high-grade healing potion she had given Damien earlier had restored most of his injuries. Even so he wasn’t in any condition to accompany her into an unknown battlefield. Without another word Morgana stepped off the branch.","She didn’t fall. She kicked against the air itself. Her figure became a blur. While descending, she drew her spear from her storage ring.","Dark mana erupted around the weapon. The black aura surrounding its blade distorted the air itself.","Below another wave of pale monsters charged out of the floating portal. Their grotesque roars echoed throughout the clearing.","Morgana swung her spear.","A massive crescent of absolute darkness exploded forward.","SHRRRRK!!","The attack swept across the battlefield. Every monster caught in its path was cut cleanly in half. Dozens of bodies collapsed before they even realized they had been struck.","Without slowing her momentum. Morgana bent her knees upon landing. Then launched herself upward.","Her destination the portal itself. With a sharp motion. She hurled her spear. The weapon shot forward like a bolt of black lightning.","A trail of dark smoke lingered behind it. The spear pierced directly through an incoming monster before continuing into the glowing portal.","Morgana followed immediately behind it. Her figure disappeared into the dimensional gateway.","She stepped inside","The moment she crossed the portal. She landed within a massive underground corridor The scene before her caused even her expression to harden.","\"There are this many?\"","The passage stretched endlessly into the darkness. Every inch of it was filled with monsters. Thousands of crimson eyes immediately turned toward her.","Their deafening roars echoed throughout the corridor.","Without hesitation Morgana dashed forward. She caught her spear the instant she reached it. One smooth spin of the weapon severed every creature surrounding her.","Bodies collapsed in every direction. Yet the corridor remained packed. The monsters simply kept coming.","\"They’re endless.\"","She calmly raised one hand. Several dark-purple magic circles appeared around her.","Then another. And another. Until dozens floated throughout the passage.","Dark mana surged outward. The overwhelming pressure alone caused the front ranks of monsters to hesitate.","For the first time instinct overpowered their hunger. They sensed danger. Then Morgana closed her hand.","The spell circles erupted simultaneously.","BOOM!","BOOM!","BOOM!","Violent explosions tore through the corridor one after another.","Walls trembled. Stone shattered.","Entire groups of monsters vanished beneath waves of destructive mana.","When the explosions finally ceased. A long stretch of the corridor had been cleared completely. Only broken stone and countless monster corpses remained.","The opening would not last long.","Already another wave of creatures was rushing forward from deeper within the passage.","Morgana rested her spear across one shoulder.","\"Good enough.\"","Without the slightest hesitation.","She advanced deeper into the unknown, determined to uncover the truth behind the labyrinth—and, if fate allowed it, any clue that might lead her to Noah.","Deep Within the Labyrinth. The further Morgana advanced, the quieter the corridor became.","Not because the monsters had disappeared. But because every creature that approached her was cut down before it could even come within several meters.","Dark mana lingered around her like a cloak.","The grotesque creatures instinctively hesitated whenever she looked their way.","Yet they continued charging without end.","Minutes later the corridor finally widened. Morgana stepped into an enormous underground hall. The scene before her immediately caught her attention.","\"...\"","A colossal corpse lay in the middle of the chamber. The giant humanoid creature was over ten meters tall, its body riddled with countless wounds.","A massive hole pierced straight through its chest. Its single eye had long since lost its light.","\"So this is the guardian Damien mentioned.\"","Her eyes narrowed. Then she noticed something even more disturbing.","The giant’s corpse trembled. Its torn chest cavity writhed unnaturally.","One after another. The pale creatures crawled out from inside the dead body.","\"Is there some kind of gate inside that body? How can so many monsters come out from it?\"","Morgana muttered quietly.","Her gaze remained fixed on the giant’s body. The creatures simply kept coming.","There was no sign of the flow slowing.","If this continued soon entire city would be covered by this monsters.","She stepped past the giant corpse. Ahead stood the stone platform Damien had described.","\"The slab...\"","She walked toward it. With a wave of her hand. A spherical barrier of mana expanded around the platform.","Every monster that entered its range was instantly repelled, allowing her a few precious moments to investigate.","Morgana slowly ran her fingers across the surface.","\"...\"","Her brows gradually furrowed.","\"This isn’t right.\"","According to Damien. A massive portal had appeared above this very platform after Noah defeated the guardian.","Yet there was no dragon carving. It was an ordinary stone slab. Almost as though the dragon altar Damien described had never existed in the first place.","\"Another inconsistency...\"","She quietly murmured. She carefully examined every inch of the platform. Searching for hidden mechanisms. Residual mana.","\"Noah...If you really were taken somewhere...\"","She slowly looked back toward the corpse producing the monsters.","She sighed.","Morgana’s expression became increasingly grim. Destroying the monsters accomplished nothing.","She had to find the source. Otherwise the horde would never end.","---","Several hours later.","Morning quietly arrived.","Warm sunlight streamed through the open veranda, illuminating the peaceful wooden house with a soft golden glow.","The storm had completely vanished. The air smelled fresh after the night’s rain. Inside the room. Noah slowly stirred. \"Mmm...\"","His eyelids fluttered. A long yawn escaped him. \"Yaaawn...\"","He lazily stretched both arms above his head before sitting upright.","\"That was...a good night’s sleep.\"","For the first time in what felt like forever. His body felt rested. The pain hadn’t disappeared entirely, but the night’s sleep had eased much of the exhaustion weighing him down.","He rubbed his eyes absentmindedly.","Still half awake.","Creak.","The faint sound of a sliding door echoed somewhere near the entrance.","Noah froze. Every trace of drowsiness vanished instantly.","His blue eyes sharpened.","\"Someone’s here.\"","Almost instinctively a sword appeared in his hand from his storage ring. He tightened his grip.","His breathing slowed. He hesitated. \"No. If it’s the owner. Pointing a weapon at them is probably the worst first impression I could make.\"","After a brief moment of thought. He lowered the sword. The blade disappeared back into his storage ring. Instead, he remained standing quietly in the middle of the room.","Alert. Ready to react if necessary.","Yet making no hostile move.","Tap.","A soft footstep echoed through the wooden corridor.","Tap.","The person was approaching the room.","Noah unconsciously swallowed. His heart began beating faster.","’Who could possibly live in a place like this...?’","The footsteps drew closer.","Tap.","They stopped just outside the open doorway. Silence filled the room. Noah held his breath. His eyes remained fixed on the entrance. Waiting for the mysterious owner of the house to finally reveal themselves."]}]);
